E["npc:ashlan-stonesmirk"] = {t="npc",n="Ashlan Stonesmirk",z="lochmodan",s="Ashlan Stonesmirk is a dwarven explosives expert assigned to the regiment guarding Dun Modr and the Thandol Span in the northern Wetlands. From there, he keeps a vigilant eye on regional dangers threatening the realm of Ironforge.",h="Ashlan Stonesmirk is a dwarven explosives expert assigned to the regiment guarding Dun Modr and the Thandol...",sec={{t="A Scout on the Border",b="Positioned at Dun Modr in the northern Wetlands, Ashlan Stonesmirk stands watch over the turbulent borderlands leading up to the Thandol Span. The northern roads are besieged by dark iron dwarves, roving troggs, and dangerous ogre encampments. Stonesmirk serves as a vital contact for Ironforge's scouting network, gathering intelligence and dispatching capable adventurers to investigate looming perils that could spill over into the heart of Khaz Modan.",sp=0},{t="A Dark Threat Looms",b="Stonesmirk plays a key role in tracking the nefarious schemes creeping across the northern border. When sinister plots threaten to undermine dwarven defenses at Dun Modr, Ashlan steps in to coordinate investigative strikes, ensuring that encroaching shadows are exposed and eliminated before they can overwhelm the local garrisons.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Ashlan Stonesmirk?",a="In this era, Ashlan Stonesmirk is stationed at Dun Modr in the northern Wetlands, near the Thandol Span.",al={"ashlan location","where is ashlan stonesmirk","ashlan stonesmirk loc"}},{q="What is Ashlan Stonesmirk's role?",a="He is an Ironforge scout tasked with observing northern border threats, coordinating field intelligence, and directing adventurers against dangerous hostile factions in the area.",al={"who is ashlan stonesmirk","ashlan purpose","what does ashlan do"}},{q="What quests does Ashlan offer?",a="He assists adventurers during the investigation of 'A Dark Threat Looms', identifying the strange powder Chief Engineer Hinderweir sends him as Seaforium and explaining how to defuse it.",al={"ashlan quests","quests from ashlan stonesmirk"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Stonesmirk represents the far-flung scouts of Ironforge defending Khaz Modan's borders against subterranean and northern incursions.",["faction:Alliance"]="Assisting Ashlan secures the strategic corridor connecting Loch Modan to the Wetlands and northern Alliance territories."},kw={"a dark threat looms","ashlan","dun modr","ironforge","loch modan","scout","stonesmirk"},rel={"subzone:dun-modr","zone:lochmodan","quest:161","topic:dwarf","subzone:mo-grosh-stronghold"},src={"Ashlan Stonesmirk"}}
E["npc:bailor-stonehand"] = {t="npc",n="Bailor Stonehand",z="lochmodan",s="Bailor Stonehand is a skilled dwarven smith residing in Thelsamar within Loch Modan. Renowned for his metallurgical expertise, he once mentored the human weaponsmith Jordan Stilwell and produces a specialized alloy crucial for masterwork armaments. Currently, his forge work faces setbacks after local Mo'grosh ogres ambushed and stole his ore shipments.",h="Bailor Stonehand is a skilled dwarven smith residing in Thelsamar within Loch Modan.",sec={{t="Master of the Forge",b="Operating in the dwarven settlement of Thelsamar, Bailor Stonehand represents the enduring craft of Loch Modan's blacksmiths. Known for his keen eye for raw minerals and his ability to smelt specialized alloys, Bailor's knowledge extends beyond Khaz Modan. He served as a mentor to the renowned human smith Jordan Stilwell, teaching him the foundational arts of metallurgy and sharing formulas that would later prove essential in forging blessed paladin armaments such as Verigan's Fist.",sp=0},{t="Ogre Ambush",b="Despite his quiet mastery, Bailor's trade is not immune to the rising threats in Loch Modan. Shipments of high-grade ore destined for his forge have fallen prey to the Mo'grosh ogres entrenched in the hills to the northeast. Without raw materials, Bailor finds himself unable to craft his rare alloys, forcing him to rely on passing travelers and allies to reclaim his stolen supplies from the brute encampments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bailor Stonehand?",a="Bailor Stonehand is a veteran dwarven smith located in Thelsamar in Loch Modan. He is known for smelting rare metal alloys and for his past role in teaching the craft of weaponsmithing to Jordan Stilwell.",al={"bailor stonehand","who is bailor","thelsamar smith"}},{q="What is Bailor's connection to Jordan Stilwell?",a="Bailor was once the teacher of Jordan Stilwell, a human smith based near Ironforge. Stilwell credited Bailor with teaching him the secrets of working refined ore, particularly a special alloy used to craft the holy warhammer Verigan's Fist.",al={"bailor and jordan","jordan stilwell teacher","verigan's fist smith"}},{q="What happened to Bailor's ore?",a="Bailor's raw ore shipment was intercepted and looted by the Mo'grosh ogres who inhabit the northeastern mounds of Loch Modan, leaving him without the materials needed for his specialized metallurgy.",al={"bailor ore shipment","who stole bailor's ore","ogre shipment"}},{q="Where can Bailor Stonehand be found?",a="Bailor can be found near the center of Thelsamar, the primary dwarven town situated along the main roadway in Loch Modan.",al={"bailor location","where is bailor stonehand","bailor thelsamar"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Paladins seeking to forge the legendary weapon Verigan's Fist walk in Bailor's footsteps, as his specialized alloy formula was taught directly to Jordan Stilwell for crafting the sacred hammer.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a master metalworker whose specialized alloys are renowned across Khaz Modan, Bailor embodies the traditional dwarven pursuit of perfecting rare and resilient metals."},kw={"bailor stonehand","jordan stilwell","loch modan","mo'grosh","smith","thelsamar","verigan's fist"},rel={"npc:jordan-stilwell","subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan","quest:1655","topic:dwarf"},src={"Bailor Stonehand"}}
E["npc:bingles-blastenheimer"] = {t="npc",n="Bingles Blastenheimer",z="lochmodan",s="Bingles Blastenheimer is an eccentric gnomish aviator stranded on the southeastern shores of the Loch in Loch Modan. Having crash-landed his experimental flying machine, he finds himself marooned amidst local troggs and beasts, desperate to salvage his precious tools and components.",h="Bingles Blastenheimer is an eccentric gnomish aviator stranded on the southeastern shores of the Loch in Loch...",sec={{t="A Rough Landing",b="Like many ambitious gnomish engineers, Bingles Blastenheimer took to the skies in a customized flying craft, only to discover that coming down safely is far more difficult than lifting off. After his gyrocopter malfunctioned and crashed into the southeastern shores of the Loch, Bingles survived the impact intact, but his machine shattered into scattered parts. Stranded far from Ironforge, he remains huddled near the wreckage, guarded against hungry crocolisks and hostile troggs while pleading with passing travelers to retrieve his scattered tools so he can piece his invention back together.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bingles Blastenheimer?",a="Bingles Blastenheimer is a gnomish pilot and tinkerer who suffered a catastrophic crash in his flying machine on the southeastern bank of the Loch in Loch Modan.",al={"who is bingles","bingles blastenheimer lore","who is the gnome by the lake"}},{q="What happened to his flying machine?",a="Bingles crashed his gyrocopter on the shoreline. The impact shattered the craft and scattered his essential tools, spare parts, and engine components into the surrounding wilderness and water.",al={"why did bingles crash","bingles gyrocopter","what happened to bingles plane"}},{q="Why hasn't Bingles returned to town?",a="Bingles is isolated and besieged by the dangerous predators and troggs infesting the lakeside. Without his lost tools and gear, he refuses to abandon the wreckage of his life's mechanical work.",al={"why is bingles stranded","why stay by the lake"}},{q="Where does Bingles end up after his craft is fixed?",a="In this era Bingles stays at his crash site on the southeastern bank of the Loch, waiting for adventurers to recover his missing supplies.",al={"where does bingles go","bingles lodge"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Bingles represents the quintessential gnomish drive for aerial innovation, where mechanical failure and explosions are simply treated as minor setbacks on the path to progress.",["profession:Engineering"]="Any tinkerer will recognize the plight of losing irreplaceable custom spanners and gadgets to the local wildlife after an ambitious test flight goes wrong."},kw={"bingles","blastenheimer","farstrider lodge","gnome","gyrocopter","loch modan","pilot"},rel={"quest:2038","quest:2039","subzone:the-loch","zone:lochmodan","subzone:farstrider-lodge","topic:gnome"},src={"Bingles Blastenheimer"}}
E["npc:brock-stoneseeker"] = {t="npc",n="Brock Stoneseeker",z="lochmodan",s="Brock Stoneseeker is a dwarven mining instructor based in the settlement of Thelsamar in Loch Modan. As the proprietor of Brock's School of Mining and Surveying, he instructs novice prospectors in the craft of extracting valuable ores and minerals from the earth.",h="Brock Stoneseeker is a dwarven mining instructor based in the settlement of Thelsamar in Loch Modan.",sec={{t="Master of Mining and Surveying",b="Operating out of Thelsamar, Brock Stoneseeker directs Brock's School of Mining and Surveying. In the mineral-rich hills of Loch Modan, seasoned expertise with a pickaxe and an eye for geological veins are indispensable. Brock guides aspiring miners through the foundational techniques of identifying ore nodes, extracting raw metals, and properly surveying subterranean deposits, ensuring Alliance tradesfolk can fuel Ironforge's legendary smithies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Brock Stoneseeker?",a="Brock Stoneseeker is a dwarf mining trainer stationed in Thelsamar within Loch Modan. He runs Brock's School of Mining and Surveying, teaching tradesfolk how to extract ore and survey raw mineral deposits.",al={"brock stoneseeker","who is brock","brock thelsamar"}},{q="Where can Brock Stoneseeker be found?",a="Brock resides in Thelsamar, the main dwarven town in Loch Modan, operating his mining establishment near the local tradesmen.",al={"where is brock","brock stoneseeker location","brock map"}},{q="What profession does Brock teach?",a="He is a Mining trainer, teaching travelers the basics of gathering rough stone, copper, and other early ores found scattered across the Khaz Modan countryside.",al={"what does brock teach","brock trainer type","mining trainer thelsamar"}},{q="What is Brock's School of Mining and Surveying?",a="It is Brock's training establishment in Thelsamar dedicated to teaching prospective prospectors how to safely extract minerals and read subterranean veins throughout the mountains.",al={"brocks school","school of mining thelsamar"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Miners traveling through Loch Modan seek out Brock Stoneseeker in Thelsamar to begin or advance their training in unearthing and smelting regional ores.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves of Khaz Modan, stone and metal are foundational, making teachers like Brock a vital link in sustaining Ironforge's deep-rooted craft traditions."},kw={"brock stoneseeker","loch modan","mining trainer","school of mining","thelsamar"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan","topic:dwarf","quest:6387","quest:6392"},src={"Brock Stoneseeker"}}
E["npc:captain-rugelfuss"] = {t="npc",n="Captain Rugelfuss",z="lochmodan",s="Captain Rugelfuss is a stern dwarven officer stationed at the southern gate in the Valley of Kings. Tasked with securing the border of Loch Modan, he organizes the defense against a sudden and aggressive trogg uprising.",h="Captain Rugelfuss is a stern dwarven officer stationed at the southern gate in the Valley of Kings.",sec={{t="Holding the Southern Gate",b="Positioned near the monumental carved arches of the Valley of Kings, Captain Rugelfuss oversees the southern gateway into Loch Modan. With Alliance forces stretched thin across the world, Ironforge relies on veteran officers like him to keep the home territories secure. Rugelfuss dismisses military pomp and formalities, preferring to focus entirely on the grim reality facing the border.",sp=0},{t="The Trogg Incursion",b="The primary crisis demanding Rugelfuss's attention is the swelling trogg threat. Unearthed from ancient caverns and surging into the highlands, these savage brutes have overwhelmed outlying dwarven patrols and established fortified footholds nearby. Under the banner of defending the King's lands, the captain recruits capable travelers to cull their ranks and push the creatures back from the roadway.",sp=0},{t="Frontline Reconnaissance",b="Rugelfuss's duties extend beyond blunt force. His mountaineers continually scout trogg encampments.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Rugelfuss?",a="Captain Rugelfuss is an Ironforge dwarven military commander stationed at the southern gateway in the Valley of Kings within Loch Modan. He is responsible for regional defense and frontier security.",al={"captain rugelfuss lore","who is rugelfuss","rugelfuss loch modan"}},{q="Where can Captain Rugelfuss be found?",a="He is stationed near the South Gate in the Valley of Kings, guarding the southern pass that leads from Loch Modan toward the Badlands.",al={"where is rugelfuss","captain rugelfuss location"}},{q="Why is Captain Rugelfuss concerned about troggs?",a="A recent trogg uprising poses a severe hazard to dwarven settlements and supply lines. The troggs have encroached directly on the southern gateway and attacked Ironforge patrols, threatening to overrun the King's territory if left unchecked.",al={"why fight troggs","trogg threat loch modan"}},{q="What is his relationship with Thelsamar?",a="Rugelfuss communicates regularly with the garrison and leadership in Thelsamar, exchanging status reports to coordinate the overall military defense of Loch Modan.",al={"rugelfuss thelsamar","south gate status report"}},{q="Why does Rugelfuss brush off military formalities?",a="Rugelfuss views unnecessary salute and ceremony as dangerous distractions when the King's lands are actively besieged. He demands immediate, practical action over protocol.",al={"rugelfuss personality","at ease race"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Captain Rugelfuss represents the steadfast resolve of Ironforge's military, standing guard over ancestral mountain passes against ancestral subterranean foes.",["faction:Alliance"]="Rugelfuss reminds Alliance travelers that while major armies fight elsewhere, defending the domestic homelands from savage incursions is critical to the alliance's survival.",["class:Warrior"]="Warriors will find common ground in Rugelfuss's no-nonsense tactical demeanor and straightforward mandate to clear the frontlines with blade and shield."},kw={"captain rugelfuss","ironforge guard","loch modan","mountaineer","rugelfuss","thelsamar","trogg threat","valley of kings"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-kings","zone:lochmodan","quest:217","quest:267","npc:captured-mountaineer","subzone:thelsamar","topic:trogg","topic:dwarf"},src={"Captain Rugelfuss"}}
E["npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii"] = {t="npc",n="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",z="lochmodan",s="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII is a veteran dwarven engineer stationed atop the Stonewrought Dam in Loch Modan. Tasked with the upkeep and defense of this monumental feat of engineering, he oversees its delicate mechanisms while keeping watch for sabotage. Those who speak with him quickly discover that grave dangers threaten the integrity of the great dam.",h="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII is a veteran dwarven engineer stationed atop the Stonewrought Dam in Loch Modan.",sec={{t="Master of the Dam",b="The Stonewrought Dam is one of the crowning achievements of dwarven stonecraft and engineering, holding back the massive waters of the Loch. Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII bears the immense responsibility of maintaining its structure and operational machinery. Perched along the crest of the dam, he monitors the waterways, sluice gates, and structural stress points against the elements and local hazards.",sp=0},{t="Sabotage and Subversion",b="Running the dam is more than routine maintenance; dark forces continually test its defenses. Hinderweir uncovers signs of calculated sabotage orchestrated by hostile elements in the region. Aware that a catastrophic breach would flood the lowlands and devastate Khaz Modan's delicate infrastructure, the Chief Engineer enlists reliable Alliance adventurers to trace the conspiracy, disarm hidden explosives, and neutralize the threat before the stone gives way.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII is the dwarven supervisor in charge of maintaining and defending the Stonewrought Dam in northern Loch Modan.",al={"hinderweir","chief engineer","dam engineer"}},{q="Where can I find Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII?",a="He can be found standing along the top walkway of the Stonewrought Dam, which spans the northern edge of Loch Modan near the border to the Wetlands.",al={"hinderweir location","where is hinderweir","find hinderweir"}},{q="What is the Stonewrought Dam?",a="The Stonewrought Dam is a massive dwarven architectural wonder that holds back the waters of Loch Modan, preventing the lake from violently spilling into the lower wetlands to the north.",al={"what is the dam","stonewrought dam purpose","why is the dam important"}},{q="What threats is Hinderweir worried about?",a="Hinderweir investigates active sabotage against the dam, discovering evidence of dark plots and explosive devices planted to crack its foundations.",al={"dam threats","a dark threat looms","who wants to destroy the dam"}},{q="Why does his name include 'VII'?",a="The Roman numeral suggests a proud family lineage of dwarven engineers or architects who have served Khaz Modan over generations.",al={"hinderweir name","why the seventh","hinderweir vii meaning"}},{q="What quests does Chief Engineer Hinderweir offer?",a="He offers the quest chain 'A Dark Threat Looms', which directs adventurers to investigate tampering and protect the Stonewrought Dam from destruction.",al={"hinderweir quests","quests at the dam","a dark threat looms quest"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Hinderweir represents the solemn duty of preserving Khaz Modan's greatest stonecraft achievements against outside malice.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers can appreciate the sheer mechanical scale of Hinderweir's charge, as the Stonewrought Dam represents a peerless mix of civil architecture and mechanical control.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance cannot afford to let the dam fall; catastrophic failure would disrupt supply routes and devastate allied lands north of Loch Modan."},kw={"a dark threat looms","dwarf","engineer","hinderweir","loch modan","sabotage","stonewrought dam"},rel={"subzone:stonewrought-dam","quest:161","zone:lochmodan","topic:dwarf"},src={"Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII"}}
E["npc:daryl-the-youngling"] = {t="npc",n="Daryl the Youngling",z="lochmodan",s="Daryl the Youngling is a human hunter residing at Farstrider Lodge in the southeastern hills of Loch Modan. Eager to prove his marksmanship among veteran dwarven trackers, he challenges traveling adventurers to hone their wilderness skills and test their mettle against the local beasts.",h="Daryl the Youngling is a human hunter residing at Farstrider Lodge in the southeastern hills of Loch Modan.",sec={{t="A Human Among Mountaineers",b="Farstrider Lodge is primarily a haven for dwarven mountaineers, trackers, and seasoned outdoorsmen who watch over the wilderness of Loch Modan. Daryl stands out as a young human striving to earn his place alongside these veteran stalkers. Rather than relying on mere bravado, he actively seeks to measure his hunting instincts against other travelers, issuing challenges to hunt down the tough wild boars and beasts roaming the crags and lakeshore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Daryl the Youngling?",a="Daryl is a young human hunter stationed at Farstrider Lodge in Loch Modan. Surrounded by grizzled dwarven marksmen, he tests newcomers with hunting contests to prove their skill with beasts and tracking.",al={"who is daryl","daryl lore","who is daryl the youngling"}},{q="Where can Daryl be found?",a="Daryl stays at Farstrider Lodge, situated on the forested cliffs overlooking the southeastern shores of the lake in Loch Modan.",al={"daryl location","where is daryl the youngling","where to find daryl"}},{q="Why is he called 'the Youngling'?",a="Compared to the experienced dwarven marksmen and lodge regulars who have spent decades patrolling Khaz Modan's rugged backcountry, Daryl is relatively young and untested, still working to establish a lasting reputation as a true hunter.",al={"why youngling","daryl nickname"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Daryl speaks the language of tracking, beast behaviour, and the hunt, making his contests a natural proving ground for wandering hunters visiting Farstrider Lodge.",["race:Human"]="Finding a young human learning wilderness craft deep in dwarven territory highlights the practical camaraderie forged between Ironforge and the human kingdoms."},kw={"boar hunting","daryl","farstrider lodge","hunter","hunter's boast","loch modan","youngling"},rel={"subzone:farstrider-lodge","zone:lochmodan","quest:257","quest:258"},src={"Daryl the Youngling"}}
E["npc:huldar"] = {t="npc",n="Huldar",z="lochmodan",s="Huldar is a dwarven teamster stationed along the southern road of Loch Modan, near the shores of the lake. Tasked with hauling vital blast powder to the dig site in the south, his delivery caravan faces relentless harassment from local threats and Dark Iron saboteurs.",h="Huldar is a dwarven teamster stationed along the southern road of Loch Modan, near the shores of the lake.",sec={{t="A Powder Run in Peril",b="Hauling explosives through Loch Modan is no simple trade route. Huldar was tasked with driving wagonloads of mining blast powder down toward the southern excavation site, where dwarven archaeologists and prospectors desperately need supplies. However, the wilderness roads have become increasingly hazardous. With local wildlife, troggs, and Dark Iron infiltrators lurking near the lake's southern bend, Huldar finds himself stranded by his damaged wagon, relying on wandering travelers to safeguard the remaining powder kegs and ensure the shipment reaches the dig.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Huldar?",a="Huldar is a dwarven teamster stranded by his wagon on the southern bank of the lake in Loch Modan. He was tasked with hauling blast powder to the nearby excavation site before his supply run ran into trouble.",al={"who is huldar","huldar loch modan","wagon dwarf"}},{q="What is in Huldar's wagon?",a="His wagon carries barrels of blast powder. The explosives are desperately needed by dwarven prospectors and archaeologists working at the excavation site to the south.",al={"what is huldar transporting","huldar wagon cargo","what are the barrels"}},{q="Why is Huldar stuck on the road?",a="The roads through southern Loch Modan have grown dangerous due to hostile beasts, troggs, and Dark Iron dwarf saboteurs. Huldar's shipment was ambushed, forcing him to halt and seek help to secure and deliver the remaining supplies.",al={"why is huldar stranded","huldar ambush"}},{q="Why do the Dark Iron dwarves care about his cargo?",a="The Dark Iron clan actively seeks to undermine Ironforge's presence and historical research throughout Loch Modan. Cutting off blast powder halts excavation efforts and deprives dwarven operations of defensive and industrial supplies.",al={"dark iron blast powder","why dark irons attack huldar"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Aiding Huldar directly supports the Explorer's League dig site, ensuring your kin have the powder needed to unearth ancient titan secrets.",["profession:Engineering"]="Any engineer knows the value—and the volatility—of raw blast powder sitting exposed in stranded wooden barrels."},kw={"blast powder","caravan","dark iron","excavation","huldar","loch modan","wagon"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch","quest:273","quest:309","quest:454","topic:dwarf"},src={"Huldar"}}
E["npc:jern-hornhelm"] = {t="npc",n="Jern Hornhelm",z="lochmodan",s="Jern Hornhelm is a dwarven miner affiliated with the Explorers' League, stationed in the town of Thelsamar. He coordinates vital logistics and communication between the settlement, Ironforge, and the archaeological dig site deeper in Loch Modan. Adventurers frequently assist him with shuttling mining supplies and progress reports across the region.",h="Jern Hornhelm is a dwarven miner affiliated with the Explorers' League, stationed in the town of Thelsamar.",sec={{t="Logistics in Thelsamar",b="Stationed within the rustic town of Thelsamar, Jern Hornhelm plays a key logistical role for dwarven operations throughout Loch Modan. While dwarven scholars and field teams venture out into the wilderness to unearth their ancestral past, maintaining consistent supply chains remains essential. Jern ensures that vital resources, tools, and communications reach the active dig sites safely.",sp=0},{t="Serving the Explorers' League",b="As a member of the Explorers' League, Jern bridges the gap between field archaeologists and the League's leadership in the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge. Sites such as Ironband's Excavation rely heavily on blasting powder, equipment, and regular dispatches to keep work moving forward. Jern enlists reliable travelers to navigate the trogg-infested roads and keep the dig fully operational.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Jern Hornhelm?",a="Jern Hornhelm is a dwarven miner and logistics coordinator based in Thelsamar in Loch Modan. He works on behalf of the Explorers' League to keep local excavation efforts running smoothly.",al={"who is jern","jern hornhelm identity","thelsamar dwarf jern"}},{q="Where can I find Jern Hornhelm?",a="He can be found standing outdoors in the town of Thelsamar, situated centrally in Loch Modan along the main road.",al={"jern hornhelm location","where is jern","jern hornhelm map"}},{q="What faction does Jern Hornhelm belong to?",a="Jern is aligned with the Alliance and specifically represents the dwarven Explorers' League, managing the movement of personnel and mining supplies.",al={"jern hornhelm faction","who does jern work for","is jern explorers league"}},{q="Why does Jern need blasting powder sent to the excavation?",a="Archaeological digs in the mountainous terrain require controlled demolitions to break through stubborn rock faces. Jern coordinates the delivery of specialized blasting powder to Prospector Ironband's dig site so the crew can safely uncover Titan relics and ancient stone halls.",al={"powder to ironband lore","why excavation needs powder","blasting powder loch modan"}},{q="What is Jern Hornhelm's connection to Ironforge?",a="Jern serves as a vital communications link between remote digs in Loch Modan and the high leadership of the Explorers' League located in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers, frequently dispatching field progress reports back to the capital.",al={"jern hornhelm ironforge","report to ironforge jern"}},{q="What problems are the dig sites facing in Loch Modan?",a="The sudden rise of aggressive troggs displaced from beneath the earth has severely threatened excavation efforts and blocked trade routes, making regular delivery runs dangerous without armed adventurers to escort supplies.",al={"ironband excavation problems","loch modan dig dangers","why jern needs help"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, assisting Jern directly advances the sacred quest to uncover the race's ancient Titan heritage buried deep within the mountains.",["profession:Mining"]="Miners will appreciate Jern's trade background and practical understanding of subterranean logistics, blasting, and resource hauling.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance travelers passing through Loch Modan find Jern to be an essential point of contact for securing the region and maintaining dwarven infrastructure."},kw={"blasting powder","excavation","explorers' league","ironband","jern hornhelm","loch modan","miner","thelsamar"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan","topic:explorers-league","quest:436","quest:302","quest:273","quest:298","quest:301"},src={"Jern Hornhelm"}}
E["npc:mountaineer-stormpike"] = {t="npc",n="Mountaineer Stormpike",z="lochmodan",s="Mountaineer Stormpike is an Ironforge mountaineer stationed at Algaz Station in northern Loch Modan. Watching over the mountain pass leading toward the Wetlands, he works tirelessly to keep vital supply routes safe from lurking troggs, gnolls, and kobolds. As a proud member of the Stormpike clan, his loyalty lies squarely with Ironforge and the safety of dwarven lands.",h="Mountaineer Stormpike is an Ironforge mountaineer stationed at Algaz Station in northern Loch Modan.",sec={{t="Guardian of Algaz Station",b="Perched along the northern border of Loch Modan, Algaz Station serves as a critical checkpoint before the perilous descent into the Wetlands. Mountaineer Stormpike is stationed here amid rocky crags and constant wilderness threats. His primary duty is maintaining the line of communication and keeping the roads open for travelers and supply convoys traversing through Dun Algaz.",sp=0},{t="Contending with Local Menaces",b="The northern reaches of Loch Modan are plagued by relentless pests, from kobolds infesting nearby digs to marauding gnoll packs and subterranean troggs. Stormpike routinely enlists passing adventurers to disrupt these threats, particularly targeting the kobolds whose filthy paws constantly pilfer supplies, gear, and valuable ore destined for Ironforge's war effort.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Mountaineer Stormpike?",a="He is stationed at Algaz Station, situated in northern Loch Modan along the mountain road that leads north into the Dun Algaz pass toward the Wetlands.",al={"stormpike location","where is stormpike","mountaineer stormpike loc"}},{q="Who is Mountaineer Stormpike?",a="He is an Ironforge mountaineer belonging to the renowned Stormpike clan. He serves as an outpost sentry and scout, tasked with securing the northern pass of Loch Modan against surrounding wilderness dangers.",al={"who is stormpike","mountaineer stormpike lore","who is mountaineer stormpike"}},{q="What threats does he deal with at Algaz Station?",a="The outpost faces frequent trouble from nearby gnoll bands, trogg incursions, and kobolds infesting the hillsides and quarries. Stormpike works to eliminate these threats so courier lines and caravans can pass through safely.",al={"algaz station dangers","what is attacking algaz station","loch modan north threats"}},{q="What is Algaz Station's purpose?",a="Algaz Station acts as an Ironforge outpost monitoring the border between Loch Modan and the rugged tunnels of Dun Algaz. It serves as a waystation for mountaineers patrolling the frontier and keeping the trade road clear.",al={"what is algaz station","algaz station lore","purpose of algaz station"}},{q="Is he related to the Stormpike Guard in Alterac Valley?",a="He bears the name of the prominent Stormpike clan, a dwarven lineage well known across Ironforge for their fierce warriors and prospectors, though his immediate orders keep him deployed along the passes of Loch Modan.",al={"alterac stormpike","stormpike clan connection","is he part of the stormpike guard"}},{q="What tasks does Mountaineer Stormpike give to adventurers?",a="He directs adventurers to reclaim stolen supplies from local pests, thin out encroaching threats like the kobolds, and carry military reports and shipments to nearby settlements.",al={"stormpike quests","mountaineer stormpike tasks","filthy paws quest"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For a dwarf of Ironforge, aiding a fellow mountaineer like Stormpike is an honored duty to protect Khaz Modan's interior borders from scavenging vermin.",["faction:Alliance"]="Algaz Station anchors the key overland conduit connecting Ironforge to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands, making Stormpike's vigilance essential to Alliance logistics."},kw={"algaz","dun","kobold","loch","modan","mountaineer","station","stormpike","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:algaz-station","zone:lochmodan","quest:307","quest:1339","quest:1338","topic:dwarf","topic:kobold","topic:gnoll"},src={"Mountaineer Stormpike"}}
E["npc:prospector-ironband"] = {t="npc",n="Prospector Ironband",z="lochmodan",s="Prospector Darteus Ironband is an honest, hardworking dwarven surveyor who oversees an archaeological dig in southeastern Loch Modan. Working under the banner of the Dwarven Explorers' Guild, he is determined to uncover the earthen heritage buried beneath Khaz Modan. Despite setbacks and hostile local creatures, Ironband remains committed to sending regular progress reports and uncovered relics back to Ironforge.",h="Prospector Darteus Ironband is an honest, hardworking dwarven surveyor who oversees an archaeological dig in...",sec={{t="Unearthing the Past",b="Darteus Ironband leads the dig at Ironband's Excavation Site nestled in the hills of southeastern Loch Modan. Like many field researchers in the Explorers' Guild, Ironband believes that the soil of Khaz Modan hides vital truths about the origins of the dwarven race. His camp works tirelessly digging trenches and sifting through rubble in search of ancient relics, stone tablets, and earthen artifacts. Despite the slow pace of unearthing buried history, Ironband's resolve remains unshaken, and he is always eager to recruit competent adventurers to safeguard his operation.",sp=0},{t="Frontier Troubles",b="Conducting an excavation in the rugged wilds is never quiet. The site faces relentless harassment from local troggs and wildlife, threatening the supply lines and equipment essential for the dig. Relics and valuable survey equipment are constantly at risk of being stolen or wrecked before they can be examined. Ironband relies on visiting Alliance travelers to protect the cargo shipments, keep hostile raiders at bay, and investigate missing guild contacts in the neighboring badlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Ironband?",a="Prospector Darteus Ironband is a dedicated dwarven surveyor leading an archaeological dig in southeastern Loch Modan. He operates on behalf of the Dwarven Explorers' Guild, coordinating field excavations to recover lost relics of titan and earthen history.",al={"ironband lore","who is darteus ironband","prospector ironband"}},{q="Where can I find Prospector Ironband?",a="He is stationed at Ironband's Excavation Site, situated in the hills of southeastern Loch Modan, just east of the main road heading toward the southern border.",al={"ironband location","where is ironband","ironband excavation site loc"}},{q="What is the Explorers' Guild digging for here?",a="The Explorers' Guild excavates ancient stone ruins throughout Khaz Modan to piece together the origins of the dwarven people and uncover artifacts left behind by the Titans.",al={"why is ironband digging","what are they excavating","ironband dig goals"}},{q="Why does Ironband need adventurers to protect shipments?",a="The dig relies heavily on specialized digging tools, preservation gear, and provisions transported across Loch Modan. Local troggs and aggressive beasts constantly ambush supply caravans and attempt to raid the camp's stockpiles.",al={"protecting the shipment lore","why defend the goods","ironband supplies"}},{q="Who is Agmond and why does Ironband ask about him?",a="Agmond was a fellow dwarf surveyor who went out to scout excavations further south. When contact was lost, Ironband enlisted travelers to search the Badlands to determine his fate.",al={"find agmond","who is agmond","agmond's fate"}},{q="Is Prospector Ironband related to Bardin Ironband?",a="They share a surname and both work closely with frontier dwarf operations, suggesting a kinship, though Darteus keeps his focus strictly on the business of archaeology and guild reports.",al={"bardin ironband relative","ironband family","darteus and bardin"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Prospector Ironband works on the front lines of King Magni's push to understand dwarven ancestry, making his excavation a matter of deep cultural pride for any son or daughter of Ironforge.",["profession:Mining"]="Ironband's dig uses standard pickaxes and trenching techniques familiar to any miner, relying on sharp eyes to identify worked stone and buried strata amidst the rock.",["faction:Alliance"]="Keeping Ironband's site supplied and defended helps secure the southeastern reaches of Loch Modan against trogg incursions and preserves valuable relics for the Alliance."},kw={"agmond","darteus ironband","excavation progress report","excavation site","explorers guild","ironband","loch modan","prospector","protecting the shipment"},rel={"subzone:ironband-s-excavation-site","quest:436","quest:298","quest:309","zone:lochmodan","topic:dwarf"},src={"Prospector Ironband"}}
E["npc:thorgrum-borrelson"] = {t="npc",n="Thorgrum Borrelson",z="lochmodan",s="Thorgrum Borrelson is the dwarven gryphon master stationed above Thelsamar in Loch Modan. From his roost overlooking the settlement, he tends the aerial mounts that connect the valley to Ironforge and the surrounding mountain passes.",h="Thorgrum Borrelson is the dwarven gryphon master stationed above Thelsamar in Loch Modan.",sec={{t="The Roost Above Thelsamar",b="Perched on the bluff rising immediately above Thelsamar, Thorgrum Borrelson handles aerial transport for the Alliance across Loch Modan. With trogg incursions and gnoll packs threatening overland paths, his trained gryphons provide vital transit over the jagged ridges. He maintains frequent connections back through the South Gate Pass to the Great Forge in Dun Morogh, as well as routes onward toward the Wetlands and beyond.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thorgrum Borrelson?",a="Thorgrum Borrelson is the Alliance gryphon flight master stationed in Thelsamar. He oversees aerial travel into and out of the Loch Modan region.",al={"thorgrum","thelsamar flight master","who is the gryphon master in thelsamar"}},{q="Where can Thorgrum send travelers?",a="Thorgrum coordinates flight routes linking Thelsamar to major hubs such as the dwarven capital of Ironforge, Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands, Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands, and several outposts throughout the neighboring territories.",al={"thelsamar flight paths","where can i fly from loch modan"}},{q="Why is gryphon travel important in Loch Modan?",a="Overland travel through Loch Modan is frequently jeopardized by hostile trogg warrens, gnolls, and Dark Iron scouts contesting mountain passes. Gryphons allow Alliance messengers, scouts, and adventurers to bypass these hazards quickly.",al={"why fly in loch modan","loch modan transport"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For mountaineers and defenders of Khaz Modan, Thorgrum Borrelson ensures a dependable aerial lifeline back to the high halls of Ironforge.",["faction:Alliance"]="Thorgrum's flight roost serves as an essential logistics waypoint connecting the heart of the dwarven realm to forward positions in the Wetlands and Arathi Highlands."},kw={"dun morogh","flight master","gryphon master","ironforge","loch modan","thelsamar","thorgrum borrelson"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan","quest:6391","zone:ironforge","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:arathi","topic:dwarf"},src={"Thorgrum Borrelson"}}
E["npc:valstag-ironjaw"] = {t="npc",n="Valstag Ironjaw",z="lochmodan",s="Valstag Ironjaw is an Ironforge dwarven soldier stationed within Menethil Keep in the coastal marshlands of the Wetlands. Facing the pressing dangers that plague the trade passages connecting Loch Modan and the coast, he assists in securing regional routes and keeping the harbor's garrison informed of local threats.",h="Valstag Ironjaw is an Ironforge dwarven soldier stationed within Menethil Keep in the coastal marshlands of...",sec={{t="Duty at the Keep",b="Found inside Menethil Keep in Menethil Harbor, Valstag Ironjaw serves as part of the dwarven garrison keeping watch over the lowlands. The surrounding marsh is rife with danger, from hostile Dragonmaw orcs to ravenous wildlife, making communications and supply lines difficult to maintain. Valstag helps coordinate defense efforts along the primary thoroughfares, particularly the treacherous passage cutting through Dun Algaz toward Loch Modan.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Pass",b="With the treacherous Algaz Gauntlet choked by hostile forces, travelers and supply convoys heading between Menethil Harbor and Loch Modan are under constant threat. Valstag directs capable adventurers to confront the brigands and orcs lurking in the passes, relaying crucial military intelligence back and forth between forward scouts and commanders like Captain Stoutfist.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Valstag Ironjaw?",a="Valstag Ironjaw is located inside Menethil Keep, the stone fortress situated in Menethil Harbor within the western Wetlands.",al={"valstag location","where is valstag ironjaw","valstag ironjaw npc"}},{q="What role does Valstag play in the Wetlands?",a="He is an Ironforge dwarf stationed at the keep who aids in defense operations, helping manage threats along the mountain roads that lead back into the dwarven heartlands.",al={"what does valstag do","valstag role"}},{q="Why is the pass to Loch Modan such a concern for him?",a="The Algaz Gauntlet is the vital land bridge connecting the coastal port of Menethil Harbor to Loch Modan and Ironforge. Hostile forces choking the mountain pass threaten to cut off food, troop movements, and supplies.",al={"why algaz gauntlet","valstag loch modan"}},{q="Who is Captain Stoutfist?",a="Captain Stoutfist is a senior officer stationed in Menethil Keep. Valstag coordinates with him to ensure military reports and security dispatches reach the garrison command.",al={"captain stoutfist connection","who is stoutfist"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Valstag assists in keeping the critical supply artery open between Menethil Harbor and the mountains of Khaz Modan, essential for Alliance trade and travel.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarven adventurers traveling down from Ironforge or Loch Modan, Valstag represents the forward garrison holding the vital, rain-swept western shoreline."},kw={"algaz gauntlet","captain stoutfist","loch modan","menethil harbor","menethil keep","valstag ironjaw","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-keep","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","quest:455","quest:473","npc:captain-stoutfist","zone:lochmodan","topic:dwarf"},src={"Valstag Ironjaw"}}
E["npc:vidra-hearthstove"] = {t="npc",n="Vidra Hearthstove",z="lochmodan",s="Vidra Hearthstove is a dwarven cook residing in the Stoutlager Inn in Thelsamar. Known for preparing local specialties, she frequently relies on traveling adventurers to gather regional ingredients for her famous blood sausages.",h="Vidra Hearthstove is a dwarven cook residing in the Stoutlager Inn in Thelsamar.",sec={{t="Kitchen of the Stoutlager",b="Within the bustling warmth of the Stoutlager Inn, Vidra Hearthstove tends the kitchen and helps feed the locals and travelers passing through Loch Modan. Sharing a surname with the innkeeper, she is part of the Hearthstove clan that keeps Thelsamar well-provisioned. Her signature dish, Thelsamar blood sausages, is a hearty dwarven staple that requires fresh game meats gathered from the surrounding wilderness, including boar entrails, spider ichor, and bear meat.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Vidra Hearthstove?",a="Vidra Hearthstove is a dwarf living at the Stoutlager Inn in Thelsamar. She is renowned for her cooking, especially the hearty Thelsamar blood sausages she serves to patrons and Mountaineers defending Loch Modan.",al={"vidra hearthstove lore","who is vidra","stoutlager cook"}},{q="Where can Vidra Hearthstove be found?",a="She can be found inside the Stoutlager Inn, located in the center of Thelsamar in Loch Modan.",al={"vidra location","where is vidra hearthstove","stoutlager inn vidra"}},{q="Is Vidra related to Innkeeper Hearthstove?",a="Given that they share a surname and work within the same establishment, she is believed to be closely related to Innkeeper Hearthstove as well as Lina Hearthstove, forming the core family running the inn's hospitality.",al={"vidra hearthstove family","is vidra related to the innkeeper","lina hearthstove"}},{q="What ingredients does she use for Thelsamar Blood Sausages?",a="Her famous recipe calls for a rugged assortment of local wildlife parts, specifically bear meat, boar intestines, and spider ichor harvested from the beasts roaming Loch Modan.",al={"blood sausage ingredients","what is in thelsamar blood sausages","vidra recipe"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Vidra represents the hearty, rustic culinary traditions of Khaz Modan, turning harsh local ingredients into sustaining meals for hungry adventurers and mountain patrols.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves passing through Thelsamar, Vidra's kitchen provides a comforting taste of home, embodying the Hearthstove family's staple role in keeping town morale high."},kw={"blood sausages","dwarf cook","hearthstove","loch modan","stoutlager inn","thelsamar","vidra hearthstove"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","subzone:stoutlager-inn","quest:418","zone:lochmodan","topic:dwarf"},src={"Vidra Hearthstove"}}
E["quest:1339"] = {t="quest",n="Mountaineer Stormpike's Task",z="lochmodan",s="Mountaineer Stormpike's Task is a brief Alliance courier dispatch in Loch Modan. Mountaineer Kadrell directs roving adventurers to the northern watchtower, where Mountaineer Stormpike requires a reliable runner for an assignment beyond the valley. It serves as an introduction to a longer errand that reaches into neighboring lands.",h="Mountaineer Stormpike's Task is a brief Alliance courier dispatch in Loch Modan.",sec={{t="A Watchman in Need of a Runner",b="Patrolling the roads and outposts of Loch Modan leaves the Mountaineers stretched thin against trogg incursions and roving wildlife. Mountaineer Kadrell frequently points capable travelers toward guards who cannot abandon their posts. Mountaineer Stormpike, stationed high in the northern guard tower, finds himself tied down by watch duties just when urgent private business requires a messenger to venture far beyond the region's borders.",sp=0},{t="From Tower to Distant Roads",b="Reaching Stormpike requires ascending the northern guard tower overlooking the valley. As a member of the prominent Stormpike clan, his affairs often extend past the everyday frontier defense of Thelsamar. Taking his task means agreeing to carry word and supplies across regional boundaries on his behalf, offering green adventurers their first major step out of the loch and onto the wider highways of Khaz Modan.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find Mountaineer Stormpike?",a="Mountaineer Stormpike is stationed at the very top of the northern guard tower in Loch Modan, keeping watch over the surrounding trails.",al={"stormpike location","where is stormpike","find stormpike tower"}},{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Mountaineer Kadrell, who patrols around Thelsamar in Loch Modan, starts this quest by pointing you toward Stormpike's tower.",al={"who gives mountaineer stormpikes task","quest starter","kadrell location"}},{q="Why does Stormpike need an adventurer?",a="As an active mountaineer, Stormpike cannot abandon his guard post at the tower. His personal errand requires traveling well outside Loch Modan, making an unattached adventurer the ideal courier.",al={"why need runner","stormpike problem","what does stormpike want"}},{q="What happens after reporting to Stormpike?",a="Speaking with Stormpike completes this introductory step and unlocks his follow-up errand, 'Stormpike's Order', which sends you on a delivery run to another territory.",al={"next quest","what comes after mountaineer stormpikes task","stormpike followup"}},{q="Is this related to the Stormpike Guard in Alterac?",a="Mountaineer Stormpike shares the name and blood of the renowned Stormpike clan known for the Stormpike Guard and their mining expeditions, though this particular assignment is a modest local errand.",al={"stormpike clan connection","alterac valley stormpike","is this the av stormpikes"}},{q="Do Horde players have an equivalent quest here?",a="No. Loch Modan is sovereign dwarven territory aligned entirely with the Alliance, and the Mountaineers will attack Horde travelers on sight.",al={"horde version","can horde do this"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Helping a fellow dwarf of the famed Stormpike line is a natural duty for any wanderer honoring clan ties across Khaz Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="Taking courier dispatches for regional mountaineers keeps the garrisons of Ironforge supplied and coordinated across the eastern territories."},kw={"guard tower","ironforge","loch modan","mountaineer kadrell","mountaineer stormpike","runner","stormpike's order","thelsamar"},rel={"quest:1338","npc:mountaineer-stormpike","npc:mountaineer-kadrell","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Mountaineer Kadrell",["end"]="Mountaineer Stormpike",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=1339},src={"Mountaineer Stormpike's Task"}}
E["quest:161"] = {t="quest",n="A Dark Threat Looms",z="lochmodan",s="Suspicious of sabotage at the Stonewrought Dam, Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII dispatches a courier north into the perilous Wetlands to have a sample of volatile powder examined. The courier must navigate the treacherous highway past the Algaz Gate to deliver the sample to demolition expert Ashlan Stonesmirk at Dun Modr.",h="Suspicious of sabotage at the Stonewrought Dam, Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII dispatches a courier north into...",sec={{t="A Powder of Ill Intent",b="Following disturbances around the Stonewrought Dam, Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII discovers traces of a pungent, unfamiliar compound near the foundation. Recognizing the potential for catastrophic sabotage, Hinderweir suspects the substance is a refined explosive designed to shatter dwarven masonry. Lacking specialized chemical testing equipment at the dam site, he insists on consulting a military demolitionist before jumping to conclusions.",sp=0},{t="The Road North",b="The urgent analysis requires a journey through the Algaz Gate down into the sodden lowlands of the Wetlands. With the marshes crawling with hostile wildlife, aggressive dragonkin, and Dark Iron infiltrators, the route is fraught with peril. Hinderweir urges travelers to stick firmly to the cobbled roadway until reaching Dun Modr, the fortified dwarven outpost anchoring the southern approach to the Thandol Span.",sp=0},{t="The Blast Expert of Dun Modr",b="Stationed on the front line of northern Khaz Modan, Ashlan Stonesmirk is the regiment's resident master of high explosives. Half-deaf from decades of concussive detonations, Stonesmirk's keen eye and nose immediately confirm Hinderweir's worst fears: the compound is indeed a specialized demolition charge, suggesting an orchestrated plot aimed squarely at the heart of dwarven engineering.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the strange smelling powder?",a="It is an alchemical explosive charge collected near the Stonewrought Dam. Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII suspects saboteurs intend to breach the dam walls with it.",al={"what is the powder","hinderweir powder","strange powder"}},{q="Why send the powder all the way to Dun Modr?",a="Dun Modr hosts the Ironforge military contingent defending the Thandol Span, including demolitionist Ashlan Stonesmirk. As a veteran explosives expert, he possesses the technical knowledge needed to identify specialized blast compounds.",al={"why dun modr","why ashlan stonesmirk","why go to wetlands"}},{q="Where is Ashlan Stonesmirk located?",a="Ashlan Stonesmirk is stationed in the military camp of Dun Modr, situated in the far northern reaches of the Wetlands just south of the Thandol Span.",al={"where is stonesmirk","find ashlan","stonesmirk location"}},{q="Why does Hinderweir warn to stick to the road?",a="The road descending from the Algaz Gate through the Wetlands cuts directly through territories infested with hostile beasts, raptors, gnolls, and Dark Iron saboteurs, making off-road travel extremely dangerous for couriers.",al={"why stick to road","wetlands dangers","road to wetlands"}},{q="Who is sabotaging the Stonewrought Dam?",a="The explosives belong to the Dark Iron dwarves, who seek to undermine Bronzebeard infrastructure and collapse the Stonewrought Dam to drown the valleys below.",al={"who made the powder","dam saboteurs","dark threat culprit"},sp=1},{q="Why is Ashlan Stonesmirk hard of hearing?",a="Years of working as a frontline military sapper and explosives specialist have left Ashlan with chronic ringing in his ears and severe hearing loss from blast concussions.",al={"stonesmirk deaf","why can't ashlan hear"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The Stonewrought Dam is one of the crowning jewels of Bronzebeard engineering. Any sign of a plot to shatter its masonry strikes at the pride and safety of all Khaz Modan.",["profession:Engineering"]="Identifying high-grade explosive residues requires a sapper's practiced eye, proving that even mundane powders can reveal the technical sophistication of an enemy saboteur.",["faction:Alliance"]="The highway running through Loch Modan and the Wetlands serves as a critical military lifeline between Ironforge and the northern Alliance holdings across the Thandol Span."},kw={"ashlan stonesmirk","dark threat looms","dun modr","explosive powder","hinderweir","stonewrought dam","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii","npc:ashlan-stonesmirk","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","zone:lochmodan","quest:631"},m={start="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",["end"]="Ashlan Stonesmirk",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=161},src={"A Dark Threat Looms (3)"}}
E["quest:1655"] = {t="quest",n="Bailor's Ore Shipment",z="lochmodan",s="Bailor's Ore Shipment is a task undertaken by paladins seeking refined metal for Jordan Stilwell's sanctified weapon. The shipment of alloy was plundered by the Mo'grosh ogres during an ambush along the roadway from the Wetlands.",h="Bailor's Ore Shipment is a task undertaken by paladins seeking refined metal for Jordan Stilwell's sanctified...",sec={{t="An Ambushed Caravan",b="When Jordan Stilwell required a specialized shipment of ore refined by his old friend Bailor Stonehand, the delivery never made it safely into Ironforge's hands. While winding its way southward out of the Wetlands into Loch Modan, the supply caravan was ambushed and slaughtered by the Mo'grosh ogres. The last surviving guard managed to limp into camp only to succumb to his injuries shortly after, leaving the shipment lost in ogre territory.",sp=0},{t="Reclaiming the Alloy",b="Bailor Stonehand, camped in Loch Modan, directs paladins across the waters of the Loch toward the northeastern hills. There, among the encampments of the Mo'grosh ogres, the stolen crate of alloy sits abandoned as plunder. Recovering the crate proves a paladin's resolve to venture into hostile territory, allowing Bailor to honor his original agreement with Jordan Stilwell.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bailor Stonehand?",a="Bailor Stonehand is a dwarven artisan and old friend of Jordan Stilwell who operates in Loch Modan. He is responsible for preparing and supplying the specialized alloy required for Jordan's craft.",al={"bailor stonehand","who is bailor","bailor"}},{q="Who stole Jordan's ore shipment?",a="The Mo'grosh ogres ambushed the supply caravan as it was traveling from the Wetlands into Loch Modan, killing the escorts and hauling off the cargo to their camps.",al={"who stole the ore","who took the shipment","ore thieves"}},{q="Where did the ambush take place?",a="The caravan was ambushed along the mountain road connecting the Wetlands and Loch Modan before it could reach the safety of local settlements.",al={"ambush location","where was caravan attacked"}},{q="Where are the Mo'grosh ogres located?",a="The Mo'grosh ogres have fortified camps in the rugged hills northeast of the Loch, across the water from the western settlements.",al={"where are mogrosh","ogre camp location","where is shipment"}},{q="Why is this shipment needed?",a="The shipment contains a particular alloy that Jordan Stilwell needs to forge a holy weapon for paladins completing their Test of Righteousness.",al={"why need ore","what is shipment for","purpose of ore"}},{q="What happened to the caravan guards?",a="Nearly all were killed outright by the ogres. The solitary guard who managed to escape and reach help died a few days later before a healer could save him.",al={"caravan guards","survivors of caravan"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Retrieving Bailor's alloy is an essential rite of passage during the Test of Righteousness, proving you can braving dangerous brutes to gather materials for your sacred warhammer.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Bailor's custom alloy represents the exacting metallurgical requirements Jordan Stilwell insists upon when constructing legendary armaments.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Mo'grosh ogre presence in northeastern Loch Modan remains an open threat to supply lines and caravans passing through the Wetlands pass."},kw={"bailor","jordan stilwell","loch modan","mo'grosh","ogres","ore","shipment","stonehand","test of righteousness"},rel={"npc:bailor-stonehand","quest:1653","zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch","zone:wetlands","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Bailor Stonehand",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1655},src={"Bailor's Ore Shipment"}}
E["quest:199"] = {t="quest",n="A Dark Threat Looms",z="lochmodan",s="This quest marks the moment an investigation into sabotage at the Stonewrought Dam uncovers physical evidence of foul play. After discovering a suspicious barrel hidden near the massive dwarven structure, adventurers retrieve a sample of strange smelling powder to bring before Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII.",h="This quest marks the moment an investigation into sabotage at the Stonewrought Dam uncovers physical evidence...",sec={{t="A Suspicious Discovery",b="The Stonewrought Dam stands as a monumental triumph of dwarven engineering, holding back the vast waters of the loch. However, whispers of sabotage have drawn scrutiny to the surrounding shoreline. Tucked away near the water's edge, an out-of-place barrel holds an ominous substance—a strange, pungent powder that clearly does not belong to standard dam maintenance supplies.",sp=0},{t="Alarm at the Dam",b="Taking a sample of the unknown powder and presenting it to Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII confirms the worst fears of the Loch Modan authorities. The engineer immediately recognizes that an outside force is plotting against the dam, shifting the investigation from mere suspicion to an urgent matter of regional defense.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the strange smelling powder?",a="The strange smelling powder found inside the barrel is an explosive or alchemical agent planted near the base of the Stonewrought Dam. It serves as direct evidence that an enemy is plotting to destroy or compromise the great barrier.",al={"strange powder","what is in the barrel","suspicious barrel powder"}},{q="Who is Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII is the dwarven master engineer overseeing the maintenance, integrity, and safety of the Stonewrought Dam in Loch Modan.",al={"who is hinderweir","chief engineer hinderweir","dam engineer"}},{q="Where is the suspicious barrel found?",a="The suspicious barrel is tucked away along the shoreline near the foundation of the Stonewrought Dam in northern Loch Modan.",al={"barrel location","where is the barrel","barrel loch modan"}},{q="Why is the Stonewrought Dam being targeted?",a="The Stonewrought Dam holds back the massive reservoir of Loch Modan. If breached, catastrophic flooding would tear through the Wetlands below, crippling Alliance trade routes and devastating dwarven holdings across Khaz Modan.",al={"why destroy the dam","dam sabotage","threat to loch modan"}},{q="Who left the suspicious barrel here?",a="The barrel was placed by agents seeking to destabilize dwarven lands, prompting Chief Engineer Hinderweir to launch a broader investigation into who is behind the plot.",al={"who planted the barrel","saboteurs","who put the powder"}},{q="What should I do after collecting the powder?",a="Take the sample directly to Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII atop the Stonewrought Dam so he can inspect the substance and prepare a response.",al={"what next","turn in powder","who to talk to"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The Stonewrought Dam is one of the crowning architectural feats of the Ironforge dwarves. Any threat to its integrity strikes directly at the safety and pride of Khaz Modan.",["race:Gnome"]="Gnomish minds appreciate the precision behind dwarven civil works, making the chemical nature of this crude sabotage particularly concerning.",["profession:Engineering"]="An engineer immediately senses danger upon inspecting volatile powders planted deliberately at the structural stress points of a major dam."},kw={"a dark threat looms","hinderweir","loch modan","sabotage","stonewrought dam","strange smelling powder","suspicious barrel"},rel={"quest:161","npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Suspicious Barrel",["end"]="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=199},src={"A Dark Threat Looms (2)"}}
E["quest:2038"] = {t="quest",n="Bingles' Missing Supplies",z="lochmodan",s="After crash-landing his gyrocopter into the waters of the Loch, the eccentric gnome engineer Bingles Blastenheimer was ambushed by local troggs who made off with his essential gear. Stranded on the lake's western shore, he needs his stolen wrench, screwdriver, hammer, and customized Blastencapper explosives recovered so he can repair his craft and rejoin the fight for Gnomeregan.",h="After crash-landing his gyrocopter into the waters of the Loch, the eccentric gnome engineer Bingles...",sec={{t="A Damp Descent",b="Bingles Blastenheimer was piloting his gyrocopter over Loch Modan when an unexpected crash sent him plummeting directly into the cold waters of the Loch. Surviving the impact was fortunate enough, but dragging himself ashore proved to be only half the ordeal. The troggs infesting the lake's central islands took immediate advantage of his predicament, swarming the dazed pilot and looting his most valuable belongings.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Ingenuity Under Siege",b="The marauding troggs scattered Bingles' essential gear across their island camps. Among the missing supplies are his standard field tools—a wrench, screwdriver, and hammer—alongside his prized invention, the Blastenheimer Blastencapper. While mundane salvage is bothersome enough to lose, parting with volatile high-yield explosives in a region already crawling with troggs poses an immediate danger to anyone traveling through Loch Modan.",sp=0},{t="For Gnomeregan",b="Bingles is not merely joyriding through the Khaz Modan skies; he considers himself an aerial vanguard for the liberation of his fallen homeland. With Gnomeregan currently overrun by subterranean troggs and irradiated leper gnomes, Bingles envisions a decisive aerial assault to break the enemy hold. Without his tools and blastencappers to rebuild his flying machine, however, his grand airborne campaign remains thoroughly grounded in the reeds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Bingles Blastenheimer stranded in Loch Modan?",a="Bingles crashed his gyrocopter straight into the Loch. While trying to recover from the wreck on the western banks, he was ambushed by nearby island troggs who plundered his tools and experimental ordnance.",al={"why is bingles here","how did bingles crash","bingles crash"}},{q="What supplies were stolen by the troggs?",a="The troggs made off with four key items: Bingles' wrench, screwdriver, hammer, and a specialized explosive charge known as the Blastenheimer Blastencapper.",al={"what did troggs steal","bingles supplies","what items bingles"}},{q="Where did the troggs take Bingles' gear?",a="The troggs carried the stolen gear back to their encampments on the islands situated in the northern portion of the Loch, scattering the tool buckets and explosives along the rocky shores.",al={"where are bingles tools","trogg island location","where is blastencapper"}},{q="What is the Blastencapper?",a="The Blastencapper is a proprietary explosive device engineered by Bingles Blastenheimer, intended for combat use in air strikes against the enemies occupying Gnomeregan.",al={"what is blastencapper","blastenheimer blastencapper","bingles explosive"}},{q="What movement is Bingles referring to?",a="Bingles is dedicated to the reclamation of Gnomeregan. He aims to mobilize an aerial bombardment campaign to purge the subterranean troggs and leper gnomes holding the gnomish capital hostage.",al={"what movement","for gnomeregan","bingles cause"}},{q="Why can't Bingles retrieve the supplies himself?",a="Bingles is isolated, soaking wet, and completely unarmed after surviving a catastrophic crash. Facing a fortified camp of aggressive troggs across open water without weapons or aircraft would be suicide for a solitary engineer.",al={"why doesnt bingles get them","why bingles waiting"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Every tool recovered brings the gnomish people one step closer to launching an aerial counteroffensive against the troggs and leper gnomes suffocating Gnomeregan.",["race:Dwarf"]="The trogg outbreak on the islands of the Loch threatens local trade and travel, making any strike against their camps a welcome service to the Mountaineers.",["profession:Engineering"]="Leaving specialized tools and volatile ordnance like the Blastenheimer Blastencapper in the crude hands of troggs is an affront to craftsmanship and a catastrophic accident waiting to happen.",["faction:Alliance"]="Assisting an Alliance pilot in the heart of Loch Modan secures the waterways and aids the broader strategic war effort to reclaim Khaz Modan's lost territories."},kw={"bingles","blastencapper","blastenheimer","gnomeregan","gyrocopter","hammer","loch modan","screwdriver","the loch","trogg","wrench"},rel={"npc:bingles-blastenheimer","quest:2039","zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch","topic:trogg","zone:gnomeregan","topic:gnome","topic:leper-gnome"},m={start="Bingles Blastenheimer",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=2038},src={"Bingles' Missing Supplies"}}
E["quest:217"] = {t="quest",n="In Defense of the King's Lands",z="lochmodan",s="In Defense of the King's Lands culminates with a direct strike against the leadership of the trogg incursion in Loch Modan. Dwarven scouts trace the violent infestation to Chieftain Grawmug and his brute bodyguards deep within Stonesplinter Valley. Captain Rugelfuss tasks bold Alliance adventurers with slaying the chieftain to shatter trogg morale and reclaim the realm's southern borders.",h="In Defense of the King's Lands culminates with a direct strike against the leadership of the trogg incursion...",sec={{t="Decapitating the Swarm",b="The persistent trogg menace across southern Loch Modan has proven to be more than random subterranean crawling. Captain Rugelfuss's scouts discovered that the Stonesplinter troggs are operating under the crude direction of a chieftain named Grawmug. Unlike typical scattered marauders, this pack moves with concerted aggression, threatening to overrun the King's Lands if left unchecked. By taking the fight into their lair and executing Grawmug alongside his personal bruisers, the Dwarven defenders hope to break the pack's cohesion and stem the tide.",sp=0},{t="Into Stonesplinter Lair",b="Grawmug makes his stand within a shadowy cavern tucked into the southeastern cliffs of Stonesplinter Valley. Surrounded by his most trusted brutes, Gnasher and Brawler, the chieftain presents a dangerous challenge for lone soldiers. Striking down this inner circle forces the remaining troggs into disarray, buying the beleaguered Mountaineers the opportunity they desperately need to fortify the roads and drive the beasts back into the dark depths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grawmug?",a="Grawmug is the vicious trogg chieftain rallying the Stonesplinter troggs in southern Loch Modan. Dwarven scouts identified him as the mastermind behind the organized assaults troubling the valley, keeping two formidable bodyguards, Gnasher and Brawler, at his side at all times.",al={"grawmug lore","who is the trogg leader","chieftain grawmug"}},{q="Where are Grawmug and his guards located?",a="Grawmug, Gnasher, and Brawler are entrenched inside a cave on the southeastern edge of Stonesplinter Valley in Loch Modan. They dwell deep in the cavern recesses together.",al={"grawmug location","where is grawmug","where to find grawmug"}},{q="Who is Captain Rugelfuss?",a="Captain Rugelfuss is the dwarven officer stationed at the Southern Guard Tower in Loch Modan. He oversees the defensive campaigns against the encroaching trogg incursions and issues orders to protect the territorial integrity of the King's Lands.",al={"rugelfuss","captain rugelfuss role","who gives defense of the kings lands"}},{q="Why must Grawmug's guards be slain as well?",a="Gnasher and Brawler are Grawmug's personal enforcers who never leave his flank. To eliminate the chieftain and definitively break the leadership of the trogg offensive, both heavy protectors must be defeated alongside their leader.",al={"why kill gnasher and brawler","gnasher and brawler","grawmug bodyguards"}},{q="What happens after Grawmug is eliminated?",a="Slaying Grawmug brings vital relief to Loch Modan. Without their chieftain to coordinate their raids, the Stonesplinter troggs lose organization, allowing the local dwarven militia to stand a fighting chance at holding the borders and pushing the beasts underground.",al={"outcome of killing grawmug","troggs after grawmug dies","did we save loch modan"},sp=1},{q="Why are troggs invading Loch Modan?",a="Troggs have long festered deep within subterranean chambers beneath Khaz Modan. Excavations and unsealed caverns have allowed them to boil to the surface, where they aggressively displace settlements and attack travelers on the King's roads.",al={"why are troggs here","trogg invasion loch modan","stonesplinter trogg origin"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, repelling troggs from Khaz Modan's ancient soil is a matter of homeland defense and honor, ensuring the mountain holds remain unblemished by subterranean scourges.",["faction:Alliance"]="Defending Loch Modan preserves the vital overland connection between Ironforge and the eastern frontiers, keeping supply lines secure for all Alliance forces."},kw={"brawler","gnasher","grawmug","kings lands","loch modan","rugelfuss","stonesplinter","trogg"},rel={"npc:captain-rugelfuss","subzone:stonesplinter-valley","zone:lochmodan","topic:trogg","topic:alliance"},m={start="Captain Rugelfuss",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=217},src={"In Defense of the King's Lands (Classic 4)"}}
E["quest:224"] = {t="quest",n="In Defense of the King's Lands",z="lochmodan",s="Mountaineer Cobbleflint guards the southern tower in the Valley of Kings, desperately seeking aid against the encroaching Stonesplinter troggs. With Ironforge's military stretched thin across distant fronts, the defense of Loch Modan's southern passes falls to passing Alliance volunteers.",h="Mountaineer Cobbleflint guards the southern tower in the Valley of Kings, desperately seeking aid against the...",sec={{t="A Thin Line in the Valley of Kings",b="The massive dwarven monuments carved into the mountains of the Valley of Kings loom over a garrison under severe strain. Mountaineer Cobbleflint and his fellow guards stationed at the southern watchtower face an ever-growing invasion of troggs erupting from the rock. With much of King Magni Bronzebeard's regular army dispatched abroad to support Alliance commitments, the home front relies heavily on local patrols and hired blades to prevent the province from being overrun.",sp=0},{t="The Stonesplinter Incursion",b="The subterranean threat originates within Stonesplinter Valley, a craggy ravine carving into the southern peaks of Loch Modan. Troggs and their scouts have burrowed surface-ward in massive numbers, carving out fortified camps along the valley floor. Left unchecked, their scouting parties threaten the critical roads connecting Loch Modan to the southern passes, forcing the Mountaineers to wage a continuous war of attrition.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the garrison in Loch Modan so undermanned?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard has committed large portions of Ironforge's military to distant Alliance battlefields and outposts across Azeroth. This foreign commitment leaves home territories like Loch Modan protected primarily by light patrols of Mountaineers who must call upon traveling adventurers to stem regional invasions.",al={"why so few guards","where are ironforge soldiers","why undermanned"}},{q="Who is Mountaineer Cobbleflint?",a="Mountaineer Cobbleflint is a dwarven sentry posted at the southern guard tower in the Valley of Kings. He coordinates perimeter security along the southern boundary of Loch Modan and directs counterattacks against the nesting trogg tribes.",al={"cobbleflint","who gives quest","quest giver"}},{q="Where is Stonesplinter Valley located?",a="Stonesplinter Valley lies south of Thelsamar, accessed by an entrance near the main road before reaching the massive dwarven statues in the Valley of Kings. The troggs maintain several encampments along its rocky floor.",al={"stonesplinter location","where are troggs","find stonesplinter valley"}},{q="What makes troggs such a severe threat to the dwarves?",a="Troggs are aggressive, subterranean brutes that tunnel through solid rock, bypassing conventional surface walls and fortifications. Because they can erupt without warning beneath roads, settlements, and mines, dwarven authorities view their unchecked proliferation as an existential danger to Ironforge's security.",al={"trogg threat","why fight troggs","are troggs dangerous"}},{q="Who do I speak to after helping Cobbleflint?",a="After thinning the ranks of the Stonesplinter troggs and scouts, Cobbleflint directs you to Mountaineer Gravelgaw, stationed just inside the adjacent watchtower, who manages the next phase of the patrol along the valley front.",al={"next quest","where to go after","gravelgaw"}},{q="Are the Stonesplinter troggs organized?",a="While primitive, the Stonesplinter clan demonstrates rudimentary organization by deploying specialized scouts to reconnoiter the roads alongside brutish foot soldiers who maintain defensive camps throughout the ravine.",al={"trogg scouts","are troggs smart","stonesplinter structure"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarven adventurers, answering Cobbleflint's call is a vital matter of homeland defense, ensuring that King Magni's ancestral valleys do not fall to subterranean pests while the army fights elsewhere.",["faction:Alliance"]="Helping secure the Valley of Kings demonstrates the strength of the Alliance bond, answering Ironforge's plea when dwarven troops are deployed on distant allied fronts.",["class:Hunter"]="The crags and outcroppings of Stonesplinter Valley provide ideal terrain to pick off aggressive trogg sentries and scouting parties from high vantages."},kw={"cobbleflint","gravelgaw","ironforge","loch modan","mountaineer","stonesplinter","trogg","valley of kings"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","subzone:valley-of-kings","subzone:stonesplinter-valley","quest:217","topic:trogg","quest:267","zone:ironforge","topic:alliance"},m={start="Mountaineer Cobbleflint",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=224},src={"In Defense of the King's Lands (Classic)"}}
E["quest:237"] = {t="quest",n="In Defense of the King's Lands",z="lochmodan",s="This military assignment tasks Alliance adventurers with blunting a trogg offensive in southern Loch Modan on behalf of Mountaineer Gravelgaw. With dwarven regular forces tied up in distant Alliance campaigns, local outposts must rely on volunteers to cull dangerous Stonesplinter Skullthumpers and Seers before the Valley of Kings is overrun.",h="This military assignment tasks Alliance adventurers with blunting a trogg offensive in southern Loch Modan on...",sec={{t="A Thin Defense",b="The Mountaineers stationed along the southern pass into Dun Morogh are stretched dangerously thin. With King Magni Bronzebeard committing significant dwarven military strength to the wider Alliance front, outposts like the Valley of Kings guard towers lack regular infantry. Mountaineer Gravelgaw relies on outside volunteers to run aggressive spoiling raids into Stonesplinter Valley, keeping the subterranean invaders at bay while local garrisons wait for reinforcements that may never arrive.",sp=0},{t="Stonesplinter Shamans and Brawlers",b="The Stonesplinter troggs are not mindless beasts wandering aimlessly; their war bands coordinate through brute force and crude elemental magic. Gravelgaw targets the tribe's veteran fighters—Skullthumpers—and their mystic leadership, the Seers. Neutralizing these frontline commanders disrupts the tribe's momentum, throwing their southern encampments into disarray and preventing a mass push against the Ironforge road.",sp=0},{t="Grim Tidings from the Front",b="Upon reporting your success, Gravelgaw shares sobering news: the promised dwarven reinforcements will not be arriving. Heavy casualties on the distant Alliance front have drained Ironforge's reserves, leaving Loch Modan entirely reliant on local mountaineers and passing sellswords to protect the kingdom's heartland.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Mountaineer Gravelgaw located?",a="Mountaineer Gravelgaw is stationed at the southern guard tower along the road through the Valley of Kings, guarding the pass that connects Loch Modan to Dun Morogh.",al={"gravelgaw location","where is gravelgaw","turn in gravelgaw"}},{q="Why are the dwarven Mountaineers so undermanned?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard has committed the bulk of Ironforge's standing military to the broader Alliance frontlines abroad. As casualties mount elsewhere, border posts like those in Loch Modan are left with skeleton crews forced to rely on traveling volunteers.",al={"why no dwarven guards","where are the reinforcements","ironforge army loch modan"}},{q="Where can the Stonesplinter Skullthumpers and Seers be found?",a="They congregate primarily in the southern camps of Stonesplinter Valley, situated east of the Valley of Kings. A smaller pocket of them can also be found haunting the northernmost island within The Loch.",al={"stonesplinter skullthumper location","stonesplinter seer location","where are the troggs"}},{q="Why target Skullthumpers and Seers specifically?",a="Skullthumpers serve as the primary vanguard shock-troops of the Stonesplinter tribe, while Seers wield crude magic and direct the lesser troggs. Eliminating both strips the invading force of its muscle and mystical coordination.",al={"why kill seers","why skullthumpers","trogg targets"}},{q="Where does Gravelgaw send you next?",a="Gravelgaw directs you to Mountaineer Wallbang, stationed in the southern guard tower in the Valley of Kings, to assist with the next phase of the valley's defense.",al={"next quest gravelgaw","who is wallbang","after defense of the king's lands"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For a dwarf, securing the Valley of Kings is personal: this ground honors the greatest rulers of Ironforge, and trogg feet defiling it while your kin bleed on distant battlefields is a bitter pill to swallow.",["faction:Alliance"]="This mission lays bare the high cost of the broader Alliance war effort, showing how securing distant territories has left core member homelands vulnerable to indigenous threats."},kw={"gravelgaw","ironforge","loch modan","mountaineer","seer","skullthumper","stonesplinter","troggs","valley of kings"},rel={"quest:217","quest:563","zone:lochmodan","subzone:valley-of-kings","subzone:stonesplinter-valley","subzone:the-loch","topic:trogg","topic:alliance"},m={start="Mountaineer Gravelgaw",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=237},src={"In Defense of the King's Lands (Classic 2)"}}
E["quest:250"] = {t="quest",n="A Dark Threat Looms",z="lochmodan",s="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII fears that the Stonewrought Dam is the next target of Dark Iron dwarf aggression following attacks in the Wetlands. With most of the dam's defensive garrison reassigned elsewhere, adventurers are sent to investigate Dark Iron sappers lurking around the eastern ramp.",h="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII fears that the Stonewrought Dam is the next target of Dark Iron dwarf...",sec={{t="A Vulnerable Wonder",b="The Stonewrought Dam is one of the crowning engineering feats of Ironforge, holding back the vast waters of Loch Modan. However, with the ongoing conflicts across Khaz Modan and beyond, much of the dam's security detail was reassigned to the Alliance Front. This troop shortage leaves Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII and his skeleton crew largely defenseless against coordinated assaults, right as enemy activity creeps closer to the colossal structure.",sp=0},{t="Echoes from the North",b="Hinderweir's anxieties stem from recent devastation across the northern border. Dark Iron dwarves struck with lethal coordination in the Wetlands, sabotaging the strategic Thandol Span and sack-pillaging the fortress town of Dun Modr. Observing known Dark Iron sappers skulking near the eastern ramp of the dam, Hinderweir realizes the pattern: the rogue clan has turned its sights on demolishing the Loch's lifeline next.",sp=0},{t="The Suspicious Cask",b="Scouting the lower ramparts confirms the engineer's worst fears. Hidden among the rocks where the sappers gathered sits an unattended, suspicious barrel packed with a volatile, strange-smelling powder. It stands as plain proof that the Dark Irons are actively preparing demolitions to crack the foundation of the Stonewrought Dam.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Chief Engineer Hinderweir worried about the dam?",a="Dark Iron forces recently devastated northern garrisons by damaging the Thandol Span and pillaging Dun Modr. Seeing Dark Iron sappers skulking along the eastern ramp of the Stonewrought Dam convinced Hinderweir that the dam is their next target.",al={"why hinderweir worried","threat to stonewrought dam","why attack the dam"}},{q="Where did the dam's garrison go?",a="Most of the security forces stationed at the Stonewrought Dam, including Hinderweir's top inspector, were reassigned to support the wider Alliance Front, leaving the critical installation thinly defended.",al={"why are there no guards at the dam","dam security detail","where are the soldiers"}},{q="What do you find at the eastern ramp?",a="Near the eastern ramp where the Dark Iron sappers were spotted, investigators uncover a suspicious barrel filled with a strange-smelling powder, confirming that the Dark Irons are planting explosives to sabotage the structure.",al={"what is the clue","suspicious barrel clue","what are the sappers doing"},sp=1},{q="What is the strategic significance of the Stonewrought Dam?",a="The Stonewrought Dam controls the reservoir of Loch Modan. If breached, the deluge would cause immense devastation downstream into the Wetlands while draining the heartland of the dwarven territory.",al={"why destroy the dam","what happens if the dam breaks","dam lore"}},{q="What was the attack on Dun Modr mentioned by Hinderweir?",a="Dun Modr was a fortified dwarven outpost in the northern Wetlands, near the Thandol Span. Dark Iron infiltrators overwhelmed the town and struck the nearby Thandol Span, severing critical overland supply routes.",al={"dun modr attack","what happened at dun modr","thandol span destruction"}},{q="Who are the Dark Iron dwarves targeting Loch Modan?",a="The Dark Iron clan has long been bitter rivals of the Bronzebeard dwarves since the War of the Three Hammers. Operating out of Blackrock Mountain and the Searing Gorge, they frequently sabotage Bronzebeard infrastructure and border defenses.",al={"who are the dark irons","dark iron sappers motive","why do dark irons hate ironforge"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The Stonewrought Dam is a masterwork of dwarven craftsmanship and pride; seeing it threatened by treacherous Dark Iron kin makes the investigation a matter of national defense.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers can appreciate both the breathtaking scale of the dam and the insidious danger represented by sappers deploying volatile chemical explosives against load-bearing foundations.",["faction:Alliance"]="With frontline armies drawn thin across the continent, Alliance recruits must step into the void to protect vital rear-guard supply hubs and regional infrastructure."},kw={"dark iron","dun modr","hinderweir","loch modan","sappers","stonewrought dam","suspicious barrel","thandol span"},rel={"npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii","zone:lochmodan","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","quest:631","topic:alliance"},m={start="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",["end"]="Suspicious Barrel",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=250},src={"A Dark Threat Looms"}}
E["quest:255"] = {t="quest",n="Mercenaries",z="lochmodan",s="Mercenaries is a bounty contract issued by Magistrate Bluntnose in Thelsamar to cull the encroaching Mo'grosh ogres in northeastern Loch Modan. With military reinforcements from Ironforge bogged down in months of bureaucratic delay, the magistrate is forced to hire passing adventurers to protect the valley's vulnerable settlements, excavations, and the vital Stonewrought Dam.",h="Mercenaries is a bounty contract issued by Magistrate Bluntnose in Thelsamar to cull the encroaching Mo'grosh...",sec={{t="Ironforge's Slow Wheels",b="Thelsamar is feeling the sting of dwarven bureaucracy. It took two full months for Ironforge to even promise a handful of soldiers to bolster Loch Modan's local defense, and another two months before those troops are slated to arrive. With town guards stretched to their limits, Magistrate Bluntnose cannot afford to wait four months while hostile forces mass just beyond the valley's borders.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in the Hills",b="The Mo'grosh ogres have fortified an encampment in the hills northeast of the loch. Their growing presence jeopardizes not just the town of Thelsamar, but the Ironband Excavation Site and the Stonewrought Dam itself. Should the dam be attacked or compromised, the devastation downstream would be catastrophic. Lacking official mountaineer detachments, Bluntnose has turned to freelance mercenaries to thin out the ogre ranks and buy the valley time against both ogres and troggs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Magistrate Bluntnose hiring mercenaries instead of using guards?",a="Ironforge has been agonizingly slow to respond to Loch Modan's pleas for aid. It took two months for the Senate to approve sending even a handful of soldiers, and another two months until they actually arrive. Facing immediate threats to Thelsamar, the dam, and local dig sites, Bluntnose has no choice but to pay independent adventurers.",al={"why hire mercenaries","thelsamar guards","ironforge help"}},{q="Where are the Mo'grosh ogres located?",a="The Mo'grosh ogres inhabit the Mo'grosh Stronghold, situated in the rugged bluffs and hills northeast of Loch Modan's great lake.",al={"ogre location","where are mogrosh","mogrosh camp"}},{q="Why is the Stonewrought Dam considered in danger?",a="The Stonewrought Dam regulates the entire lake and is an architectural jewel of the dwarves. With military defense practically nonexistent and the Mo'grosh ogres establishing a camp nearby, Bluntnose fears an organized raid could damage or sabotage the massive structure, unleashing catastrophic floods.",al={"why protect dam","ogres and the dam"}},{q="What other threats does Thelsamar face alongside the ogres?",a="Troggs have erupted across the loch from underground ruins and excavations. Bluntnose considers them a massive menace, but the brute strength of the nearby ogre stronghold forces him to hire fighters to push back the Mo'grosh so the local guard can concentrate on the trogg incursions.",al={"other threats loch modan","trogg threat"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing the crown jewel of dwarven engineering—the Stonewrought Dam—left unguarded due to Ironforge red tape makes Bluntnose's call to arms a personal matter for any mountaineer or traveler from the capital.",["faction:Alliance"]="Loch Modan forms a crucial corridor between Khaz Modan and the northern kingdoms; letting it fall into chaos under ogre raids threatens Alliance supply lines across the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"loch modan","magistrate bluntnose","mercenaries","mo'grosh","ogre","stonewrought dam","thelsamar"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan","zone:ironforge","topic:trogg","topic:light"},m={start="Magistrate Bluntnose",level="19",faction="Alliance",id=255},src={"Mercenaries"}}
E["quest:256"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Chok'sul",z="lochmodan",s="A bounty posted in Thelsamar by Magistrate Bluntnose calls for the death of Chok'sul, an ogre warlord menacing northeastern Loch Modan. Believed to be organizing the assaults against local settlements and critical infrastructure, bringing his head secures a handsome reward from the town's leadership.",h="A bounty posted in Thelsamar by Magistrate Bluntnose calls for the death of Chok'sul, an ogre warlord...",sec={{t="A Threat to the Loch",b="While troggs and wildlife constantly test the borders of Loch Modan, the arrival of organized ogres represents an escalation that the local dwarven mountaineers cannot ignore. Settling into encampments along the rugged northeastern reaches of the valley, these brutes have moved beyond simple scavenging. According to local scouts and town authorities, their raids are focused, persistent, and dangerous.",sp=0},{t="The Price on Chok'sul's Head",b="Thelsamar's Magistrate Bluntnose identified Chok'sul as the mastermind coordinating the violence against the town, the nearby dwarven excavation site, and the Stonewrought Dam itself. Fearing catastrophic damage to the valley's prized engineering feat and civilian lives, the magistrate placed a bounty upon the ogre chieftain: dead through any means necessary, with his severed head required as proof.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who posted the bounty on Chok'sul?",a="Magistrate Bluntnose, the chief civic official of Thelsamar, officially issued the order on behalf of the town to protect the region from organized raids.",al={"who wants choksul dead","who posted choksul bounty","thelsamar wanted poster"}},{q="Why is Chok'sul considered such a high priority target?",a="Chok'sul is believed to be the coordinator directing ogre strikes against Thelsamar, the Ironforge archaeological excavations, and the Stonewrought Dam—targets that represent both dwarven lives and critical kingdom infrastructure.",al={"why kill choksul","what did choksul do","choksul threat"}},{q="Where can Chok'sul be found?",a="He is located in the ogre encampment situated among the rugged hills in the northeastern corner of Loch Modan.",al={"choksul location","where is choksul","ogre camp loch modan"}},{q="What proof does Magistrate Bluntnose require?",a="You must take Chok'sul's severed head directly to Magistrate Bluntnose inside Thelsamar to claim the bounty and Ironforge's gratitude.",al={"choksul head","bounty proof","turn in choksul"}},{q="Why would ogres attack the Stonewrought Dam?",a="The Stonewrought Dam holds back the massive lake of Loch Modan and is a crowning marvel of dwarven engineering. Sabotaging it would flood the wetlands and devastate dwarven supply lines, making it a prime tactical target for hostile forces.",al={"why attack the dam","stonewrought dam under attack"}},{q="Are there other ogres working with Chok'sul?",a="Yes, Chok'sul commands an encampment of ogres established in the northeastern hills of the loch, directing their raids across the surrounding territories.",al={"choksul clan","loch modan ogres","choksul followers"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Defending the Stonewrought Dam and the surrounding archaeological digs strikes directly at dwarven pride, heritage, and the security of Ironforge's sovereign lands.",["faction:Alliance"]="Loch Modan acts as a primary agricultural and supply corridor leading into Dun Morogh, making stability around Thelsamar essential to Alliance military efforts.",["profession:Engineering"]="The Stonewrought Dam is one of the greatest feats of dwarven civil engineering ever constructed; allowing brute ogres to damage it is unthinkable to any respectable craftsman."},kw={"bluntnose","bounty","chok'sul","choksul","loch modan","ogre","stonewrought dam","thelsamar"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","subzone:stonewrought-dam","zone:lochmodan","zone:ironforge"},m={start="WANTED",["end"]="Magistrate Bluntnose",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=256},src={"WANTED: Chok'sul"}}
E["quest:257"] = {t="quest",n="A Hunter's Boast",z="lochmodan",s="A Hunter's Boast is a timed hunting challenge issued by Daryl the Youngling at Farstrider Lodge in Loch Modan. Eager to flaunt his supposed mastery, the arrogant young dwarf dares adventurers to track and slay six mountain buzzards before his fifteen-minute timer expires.",h="A Hunter's Boast is a timed hunting challenge issued by Daryl the Youngling at Farstrider Lodge in Loch Modan.",sec={{t="A Young Marksman's Arrogance",b="Farstrider Lodge serves as a gathering ground for some of Khaz Modan's finest trackers and marksmen, but not everyone under its roof possesses veteran humility. Daryl the Youngling—who fancies himself 'Daryl the Bold'—is quick to dismiss wandering adventurers. Convinced that greenhorn outsiders cannot hold a candle to dwarven hunting prowess, he lays down a brash wager: bag half a dozen local mountain buzzards within a quarter of an hour, or admit defeat.",sp=0},{t="Thinning the Scavengers",b="Mountain buzzards circle the crags and hillsides of Loch Modan, scavenging scraps and preying on smaller wildlife. While dangerous in numbers, they serve primarily as a baseline test of a hunter's speed, patience, and aim. Those who bring down the required quarry within the strict time limit quickly deflate Daryl's puffed-up pride, forcing him to reluctantly part with one of his ranged weapons and setting the stage for further hunting dares.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this hunting challenge take place?",a="The quest begins at Farstrider Lodge, situated in the southeastern wilderness of Loch Modan. The mountain buzzards you must hunt roam the nearby crags and open ridges across the zone.",al={"quest location","where is daryl","where are buzzards"}},{q="Who is Daryl the Youngling?",a="Daryl the Youngling is an ambitious, boastful dwarven youth staying at Farstrider Lodge. Calling himself 'Daryl the Bold,' he enjoys taunting travelers into timed hunting trials to prove his own imagined superiority.",al={"who is daryl","daryl the bold lore","daryl farstrider"}},{q="Why is there a time limit on the hunt?",a="The fifteen-minute restriction is part of Daryl's wager. He believes that taking down wild raptors under pressure is a feat well beyond an ordinary adventurer's skill.",al={"why 15 minutes","timer on quest","timed trial"}},{q="What happens after beating Daryl's challenge?",a="Though shocked by your success, Daryl refuses to admit true defeat. He honors his wager by offering a weapon, then immediately offers another hunting task—A Hunter's Challenge—targeting larger game.",al={"what comes next","boast followup","hunter chain"},sp=1},{q="Why hunt mountain buzzards specifically?",a="Flocks of mountain buzzards nest around Loch Modan's rocky slopes. They serve as an agile, flying target ideal for testing whether an archer or rifleman has genuine field discipline.",al={"why buzzards","buzzard purpose","loch modan buzzards"}},{q="Does this quest tie into the rest of Farstrider Lodge's tasks?",a="Yes. Daryl's tests lead directly into a broader sequence of hunts for the lodge, culminating in tracking down Ol' Sooty, the bear that scarred Daryl, as part of Vyrin Swiftwind's plan to get back at the boastful youngster.",al={"vyrin connection","lodge story","farstrider storyline"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="For marksmen and trackers, Daryl's contest is an amusing chance to outshoot a boasting novice on his home turf and claim a reliable bow or gun.",["race:Dwarf"]="Fellow mountaineers will recognize Daryl's posturing as classic youthful dwarven bravado, best answered with quiet competence.",["faction:Alliance"]="Farstrider Lodge serves as an important Alliance outpost along the southeastern roads of Loch Modan, providing shelter and staging hunts across the rugged valleys."},kw={"a hunter's boast","daryl the bold","daryl the youngling","farstrider lodge","hunting challenge","loch modan","mountain buzzards","timed quest"},rel={"npc:daryl-the-youngling","subzone:farstrider-lodge","quest:258","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Daryl the Youngling",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=257},src={"A Hunter's Boast"}}
E["quest:258"] = {t="quest",n="A Hunter's Challenge",z="lochmodan",s="A Hunter's Challenge is a timed hunting trial issued by the brash dwarf Daryl the Youngling at Farstrider Lodge in southeastern Loch Modan. Annoyed by his own inability to belittle your previous success, Daryl wagers the shirt off his back that you cannot track and fell five elder mountain boars within twelve minutes. The task tests an adventurer's swiftness against the rugged terrain and dangerous wildlife of the highlands.",h="A Hunter's Challenge is a timed hunting trial issued by the brash dwarf Daryl the Youngling at Farstrider...",sec={{t="A Youth's Boast",b="Daryl the Youngling resides among the seasoned huntsmen of Farstrider Lodge, yet he carries none of their quiet patience. Instead, Daryl compensates for his lack of years with bluster and exaggerated hunting tales, including rambling yarns about how he earned his 'famous' scar. Unwilling to acknowledge anyone else's competence, he continuously botches his fellow hunters' names and devises strict trials meant to humble newcomers and restore his own inflated standing among the lodge's residents.",sp=0},{t="The Highland Hunt",b="Unlike the simpler boars of Coldridge Valley where fledgling dwarven scouts first learn their trade, the elder mountain boars wandering the crags and hillsides of Loch Modan are massive, thick-skinned, and dangerous when provoked. Daryl gives hunters a mere twelve minutes to locate, dispatch, and confirm the kill of five such beasts. Completing the hunt swiftly enough forces the loudmouthed youngster into an awkward retreat, feigning ignorance of the extravagant wager he so casually made.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Daryl the Youngling?",a="Daryl is a young, boastful dwarven huntsman living at Farstrider Lodge in southeastern Loch Modan. Desperate to appear as formidable as the older veterans around him, he incessantly talks up his own prowess, invents grand tales, and challenges passing adventurers to difficult hunting trials.",al={"who is daryl","daryl youngling lore","farstrider lodge daryl"}},{q="Where are the elder mountain boars located?",a="Elder mountain boars roam the foothills, meadows, and ridges surrounding Farstrider Lodge and the southern and eastern expanses of Loch Modan. They can be found grazing throughout the rolling high ground between the lodge and the central loch.",al={"elder mountain boar location","where to find boars","boar hunt area"}},{q="Why is this hunt timed?",a="Daryl limits the hunt to twelve minutes because he fully expects you to fail. By setting a tight deadline, he hopes to embarrass you and prove that your earlier hunting accomplishments were nothing more than beginner's luck.",al={"why twelve minutes","why is it timed","hunter challenge timer"}},{q="What bet did Daryl make?",a="While explaining the trial, Daryl boldly proclaimed he would give you the very shirt off his back if you managed to slay the five elder mountain boars in time. Naturally, upon your triumphant return, he quickly pretends to have no recollection of any such wager.",al={"daryl's bet","shirt off his back","what did daryl wager"}},{q="How does this compare to Coldridge Valley boars?",a="Daryl specifically points out that these elder mountain boars are far tougher and more aggressive than the small, tame boars novice dwarves hunt in Coldridge Valley. Loch Modan's mature boars possess thicker hides and dangerous tusks honed on highland granite.",al={"coldridge boars vs mountain boars","coldridge comparison"}},{q="Where does this hunting chain lead next?",a="Once you silence Daryl's boasting by finishing his challenge, attention at the lodge shifts toward more serious business, leading into a confrontation with the dangerous elder bear Ol' Sooty in the quest Vyrin's Revenge.",al={"what quest is next","after a hunters challenge","hunting questline"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="For tracking specialists, tracking five elder mountain boars through the highland brush within a strict time window offers a classic test of quarry management and rapid dispatch.",["race:Dwarf"]="Any dwarf who came up through Coldridge Valley will recognize Daryl's comparison immediately, though tolerating his patronizing attitude is harder to stomach.",["faction:Alliance"]="Farstrider Lodge serves as an essential staging ground for Alliance woodsmen protecting the eastern border of Loch Modan against wild beasts and highland threats."},kw={"boar","coldridge","daryl","elder mountain boar","farstrider lodge","hunting","loch modan","youngling"},rel={"npc:daryl-the-youngling","subzone:farstrider-lodge","quest:257","zone:lochmodan","subzone:coldridge-valley"},m={start="Daryl the Youngling",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=258},src={"A Hunter's Challenge"}}
E["quest:263"] = {t="quest",n="In Defense of the King's Lands",z="lochmodan",s="This mission represents the escalating fight waged by Ironforge's Mountaineers against the trogg infestation in southern Loch Modan. Operating from the Southern Guard Tower, Mountaineer Wallbang directs seasoned recruits into Stonesplinter Valley to cull dangerous trogg shamans and front-line bonesnappers. Completing this trial earns Wallbang's full trust and opens an audience with the garrison's commanding captain.",h="This mission represents the escalating fight waged by Ironforge's Mountaineers against the trogg infestation...",sec={{t="A Thin Dwarven Line",b="Loch Modan's defenses are stretched to their limits. With dwarven regular reserves summoned to distant fronts across Azeroth, local outposts like the Southern Guard Tower are left short-handed. Mountaineer Wallbang and his few comrades face relentless pressure from the Stonesplinter clan, forcing them to rely heavily on visiting Alliance travelers to hold the southern pass.",sp=0},{t="Targeting the Stonesplinter Vanguard",b="Rather than picking off stray scouts, this campaign strikes deeper into the Stonesplinter hierarchy. The trogg bonesnappers provide the clan with brutal brute force, while their primitive shamans weave earthen magic to rally their kin. Eliminating twenty of these high-value targets blunts their incursions into the lowlands, directly serving King Magni Bronzebeard's defense of the realm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mountaineer Wallbang?",a="Mountaineer Wallbang is an Ironforge dwarf posted at the Southern Guard Tower in Loch Modan. He is tasked with monitoring trogg activity spillover from the mountains and coordinating militia efforts to keep the main southern road secure.",al={"wallbang","who is wallbang","mountaineer wallbang lore"}},{q="Why are the Mountaineers asking travelers for help?",a="Ironforge's military reserves have been called away to higher-priority battlefronts across the kingdom and beyond. This redeployment leaves border outposts like Loch Modan's southern watchtowers critically undermanned against local threats.",al={"why do dwarves need help","where are ironforge guards","why no reserves"}},{q="Where are these troggs located?",a="They concentrate heavily in Stonesplinter Valley, tucked into the rugged hills southwest of The Loch. Smaller bands of these shamans and bonesnappers also haunt the northern islands out on the lake itself.",al={"where are stonesplinter troggs","stonesplinter shaman location","where is stonesplinter valley"}},{q="What makes the Stonesplinter clan a threat?",a="Troggs reproduce rapidly and overrun settled territory through sheer subterranean swarms. The Stonesplinter clan wields crude elemental magic through their shamans and relies on ferocious bonesnappers to tear through dwarven scouts, threatening nearby settlements and trade paths.",al={"why are troggs dangerous","stonesplinter threat"}},{q="What does Mountaineer Wallbang do after this task?",a="Satisfied that you are a proven fighter in service to King Magni, Wallbang directs you to report to Captain Rugelfuss for more strategic orders in the defense of Loch Modan.",al={"what next after wallbang","who is the captain"}},{q="Who rules Ironforge during this crisis?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard rules the dwarven kingdom from the Great Forge in Ironforge. Every effort made to safeguard Loch Modan is carried out in his name and defense of his sovereign lands.",al={"who is the dwarven king","king of ironforge"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Answering Wallbang's call is a matter of home defense for any dwarf, stepping in to protect the homesteads of Loch Modan while your kin's standing armies are diverted abroad.",["faction:Alliance"]="Aiding the Southern Guard Tower shores up vital trade and travel routes connecting Dun Morogh to the eastern wetlands and the kingdom of Stormwind.",["class:Shaman"]="Facing the crude spellcasters of the Stonesplinter troggs offers an unrefined, feral look into earth magic twisted by savage instincts."},kw={"bonesnapper","ironforge","loch modan","magni","mountaineer","shaman","stonesplinter","trogg","wallbang"},rel={"quest:217","zone:lochmodan","subzone:stonesplinter-valley","topic:trogg","zone:ironforge","subzone:the-loch","topic:alliance"},m={start="Mountaineer Wallbang",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=263},src={"In Defense of the King's Lands (Classic 3)"}}
E["quest:267"] = {t="quest",n="The Trogg Threat",z="lochmodan",s="The Trogg Threat is an Alliance quest issued by Captain Rugelfuss at the Southern Gate of Loch Modan. With the local Ironforge Reserve called away to support Alliance battlefronts, the remaining defenders are stretched thin against the hostile trogg tribes in the hills. Adventurers are tasked with culling the troggs and returning with their stone teeth to relieve pressure on the mountain pass.",h="The Trogg Threat is an Alliance quest issued by Captain Rugelfuss at the Southern Gate of Loch Modan.",sec={{t="A Depleted Frontier",b="The defensive line guarding the southern approach into Loch Modan is in a precarious state. The regular dwarven mountaineers and Ironforge Reserve regiments have been dispatched to reinforce broader Alliance war fronts, leaving Captain Rugelfuss and a skeleton garrison stationed at the southern guard tower. Constrained by strict orders not to abandon the gate, Rugelfuss cannot mount an active offensive into the highlands, leaving nearby settlers and travelers vulnerable to ambushes.",sp=0},{t="Stemming the Tide",b="Troggs residing in the surrounding crags pose an escalating danger to Khaz Modan. Left unchecked, their numbers swell quickly, threatening to overrun dwarven outposts. To buy time and thin the menace, Rugelfuss calls upon wandering adventurers to assault the troggs directly in their hillside warrens and present severed stone teeth as physical confirmation of the deed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Rugelfuss?",a="Captain Rugelfuss is an officer in the dwarven military stationed at the Southern Gate guard tower in Loch Modan. He is tasked with securing the pass against intrusions while dealing with a severe lack of garrison troops.",al={"captain rugelfuss","who gives the trogg threat","rugelfuss"}},{q="Why is the Southern Gate understaffed?",a="The Ironforge Reserve has been mobilized and reassigned to fight on the larger Alliance front lines abroad. Only a small regiment remains behind at the gate, bound to their defensive post and unable to mount retaliatory strikes.",al={"why are there no guards","ironforge reserve absent","where are the dwarven soldiers"}},{q="What are Trogg Stone Teeth?",a="Troggs have naturally petrified, stone-like dental features reflective of their subterranean earthen heritage. Captain Rugelfuss demands them as unmistakable physical proof that troggs have been slain.",al={"trogg stone tooth","stone teeth","why trogg teeth"}},{q="Where are the troggs located?",a="The troggs can be found inhabiting the rocky hills, ravines, and excavation sites flanking the road near the Southern Gate in Loch Modan.",al={"where to find troggs","trogg locations loch modan","where are troggs for this quest"}},{q="Why are the troggs such a threat right now?",a="Troggs reproduce rapidly, act with violent territorial aggression, and overrun inhabited lands whenever military garrisons are diverted. Without active culling, they threaten to choke the passes connecting Loch Modan to neighboring territories.",al={"why are troggs dangerous","trogg problem","what do troggs want"}},{q="How does completing this quest aid King Magni Bronzebeard?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard bears responsibility for the safety of all Khaz Modan. By reducing the trogg population while Ironforge's armies are fighting abroad, adventurers protect the realm's internal supply lines and vulnerable frontier settlements.",al={"magni bronzebeard connection","does magni care","why help ironforge"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, culling the troggs near the Southern Gate is a direct duty to Khaz Modan and earns the praise of King Magni Bronzebeard himself.",["faction:Alliance"]="The quest highlights how Alliance commitments in distant lands have stripped local garrisons like Loch Modan of their defensive reserves."},kw={"captain rugelfuss","ironforge reserve","khaz modan","loch modan","magni bronzebeard","southern gate","trogg","trogg stone tooth"},rel={"npc:captain-rugelfuss","topic:trogg","zone:lochmodan","npc:magni-bronzebeard","zone:ironforge","topic:alliance"},m={start="Captain Rugelfuss",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=267},src={"The Trogg Threat (Classic)"}}
E["quest:273"] = {t="quest",n="Resupplying the Excavation",z="lochmodan",s="Resupplying the Excavation is an Alliance quest in Loch Modan where adventurers pursue a powder shipment meant for Ironband's Excavation Site. Dispatched by Jern Hornhelm to catch up with the pack team, the traveler discovers a dangerous ambush along the shore of the Loch.",h="Resupplying the Excavation is an Alliance quest in Loch Modan where adventurers pursue a powder shipment...",sec={{t="A Heavy Cargo along the Shore",b="Ironband's Excavation Site in southern Loch Modan requires a steady supply of blastpowder to uncover ancient titan artifacts buried deep within the mountains. After blastpowder was delivered to Thelsamar, local quartermaster Jern Hornhelm arranged for three dwarves—Huldar, Miran, and Saean—to haul the volatile barrels south along the lakeside road. Burdened by the weighty cargo, the supply party moved slowly, giving travelers in Thelsamar an opportunity to catch up and lend support on the road.",sp=0},{t="Treachery in the Shadows",b="Catching up to the pack wagon along the southern road reveals chaos rather than a routine delivery. The shipment was ambushed by Dark Iron dwarves, who actively seek to sabotage the Bronzebeard expedition's archaeological efforts. Worse than the raid itself, the attack exposed bitter treachery: Saean, a worker trusted and employed alongside Huldar for nearly a year, proved to be a Dark Iron sympathizer who assisted in organizing the ambush.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest Resupplying the Excavation?",a="Jern Hornhelm offers the quest in Thelsamar after you deliver blastpowder to him. He asks you to follow the road south along the Loch to catch up with the supply team.",al={"who gives resupplying the excavation","quest starter resupplying the excavation","where to start resupplying the excavation"}},{q="Where can Huldar and the wagon be found?",a="Huldar and the wagon are located south of Thelsamar, following the road that hugs the western and southern curve of the Loch heading toward Ironband's Excavation Site.",al={"find huldar","huldar location","where is the wagon loch modan"}},{q="Why is blastpowder being sent to Ironband?",a="Prospector Ironband and his team are unearthing ancient earthen ruins and relics at the southern excavation site. Blastpowder is needed to break apart heavy stone and blast through subterranean layers.",al={"why ironband needs powder","ironband blastpowder","why blastpowder to excavation"}},{q="Who ambushed Huldar's wagon?",a="The wagon was ambushed by hostile Dark Iron dwarves seeking to disrupt Ironforge's archaeological operations across Loch Modan.",al={"who attacked the wagon","wagon ambush loch modan","who attacked huldar"},sp=1},{q="What role did Saean play in the attack?",a="Saean was an associate working alongside Huldar and Miran for nearly a year, but the ambush revealed him to be a traitor and a Dark Iron sympathizer who aided the attackers.",al={"who is saean","saean betrayal","what did saean do"},sp=1},{q="What quest comes next after finding Huldar?",a="Speaking with Huldar completes this leg of the journey and leads directly into 'After the Ambush', where you deal with the immediate aftermath of the Dark Iron attack.",al={"next quest after resupplying the excavation","quest after huldar"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The ambush strikes close to home for Bronzebeard dwarves, demonstrating that Dark Iron infiltration runs deep within seemingly peaceful communities like Thelsamar.",["profession:Mining"]="Moving volatile blasting powder across rough terrain is hazardous enough without treachery, making this shipment essential for the excavators down south."},kw={"blastpowder","huldar","ironband","jern hornhelm","loch modan","miran","resupplying the excavation","saean","thelsamar"},rel={"npc:jern-hornhelm","npc:huldar","quest:454","quest:302","zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch","topic:dark-iron-dwarf","topic:dwarf"},m={start="Jern Hornhelm",["end"]="Huldar",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=273},src={"Resupplying the Excavation (Classic)"}}
E["quest:278"] = {t="quest",n="A Dark Threat Looms",z="lochmodan",s="This quest is a critical step in defending the Stonewrought Dam from a suspected Dark Iron plot. Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII tasks adventurers with gathering rare chemical and organic reagents from across Loch Modan to concoct a defusing mixture. Without these components, the defenders will be unable to neutralize the explosives planted beneath the massive stonework.",h="This quest is a critical step in defending the Stonewrought Dam from a suspected Dark Iron plot.",sec={{t="A Volatile Recipe",b="To counteract the volatile explosive concoctions used by Dark Iron saboteurs, Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII relies on an unorthodox chemical neutralizer. Rather than simple water or dampening sand, neutralizing Dark Iron blast powders requires a potent slurry made from indigenous Forest Lurker venom, a tear extracted from the crocolisks inhabiting the Loch, and a Mo'grosh crystal. Each component brings unique reactive properties necessary to render dwarven demolition charges completely inert.",sp=0},{t="Perilous Gathering",b="Securing these ingredients takes adventurers to the most hostile corners of Loch Modan. While the lurker spiders and loch crocolisks pose mundane natural hazards, obtaining a Mo'grosh crystal demands braving the ogre stronghold in the northeastern hills. The Mo'grosh ogres guard these rare, mined mineral formations jealously, forcing anyone seeking to protect the dam to fight their way through brute encampments to secure a sample.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Engineer Hinderweir need these specific reagents?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII is concocting a specialized neutralizing compound to defuse Dark Iron explosives. The caustic lurker venom, crocolisk secretions, and magical minerals found in Mo'grosh crystals provide the precise chemical reactions needed to render advanced saboteur charges inert.",al={"why spider venom","why crocolisk tear","defusing mixture reagents"}},{q="Where do Mo'grosh crystals come from?",a="The crystals are mined and hoarded by the Mo'grosh ogres occupying the northeastern hills of Loch Modan. Because they are considered a rare and valuable commodity by the ogres, obtaining one requires venturing into their heavily defended territory.",al={"where are crystals","mogrosh crystal location","who has the crystal"}},{q="What is the dark threat menacing Loch Modan?",a="The threat stems from Dark Iron dwarf infiltrators who seek to destroy the Stonewrought Dam. Demolishing this massive engineering marvel would flood the Wetlands below, cut off Alliance supply lines, and devastate the region.",al={"what dark threat","who is attacking the dam","dark threat looms story"}},{q="Who is Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII?",a="He is the chief dwarven engineer in charge of overseeing the Stonewrought Dam's operations and integrity. He orchestrates both structural maintenance and local defenses against sabotage.",al={"who is hinderweir","chief engineer hinderweir"}},{q="Where can the indigenous creatures be found?",a="Forest Lurker spiders roam the wooded wilderness surrounding the valley, while crocolisks dwell in and around the shores of the Loch itself.",al={"where are lurkers","crocolisk location","where to find spiders"}},{q="Why don't the Ironforge guards gather these items themselves?",a="The mountaineers and local guards are stretched thin defending towns like Thelsamar and keeping watch for Dark Iron scouts. Specialized procurement tasks and raids into ogre territory are routinely delegated to capable traveling adventurers.",al={"why help hinderweir","where are ironforge guards"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers can appreciate Hinderweir's ingenuity in formulating a chemical counter-agent capable of stabilizing volatile demolition charges in the field.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves of Khaz Modan, stopping Dark Iron sabotage at the Stonewrought Dam is a vital duty to protect their ancestral lands and architectural triumphs.",["faction:Alliance"]="Failure to neutralize the threat against the dam would result in catastrophe, severing critical overland supply routes connecting Ironforge to the northern kingdoms."},kw={"crocolisk tear","dark iron","hinderweir","loch modan","lurker venom","mo'grosh crystal","stonewrought dam"},rel={"npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii","zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch"},m={start="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=278},src={"A Dark Threat Looms (5)"}}
E["quest:280"] = {t="quest",n="A Dark Threat Looms",z="lochmodan",s="A desperate emergency mission given by Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII to prevent the destruction of the Stonewrought Dam. Dark Iron saboteurs have planted an explosive Seaforium charge deep below the waterline, threatening to shatter one of the greatest engineering marvels of the dwarven kingdom.",h="A desperate emergency mission given by Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII to prevent the destruction of the...",sec={{t="Sabotage Beneath the Surface",b="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII spotted Dark Iron Insurgents swimming toward the base of the Stonewrought Dam carrying a massive keg of explosive Seaforium. Without Mountaineers nearby to intervene, the infiltrators secured the weapon directly against the dam's underwater foundation. A breach would unleash the entire volume of the loch into the lowlands below, causing catastrophic flooding and crippling dwarven trade and travel across the region.",sp=0},{t="A Volatile Neutralizer",b="Having quickly combined reactive ingredients into a disarming mixture, Hinderweir sends a brave diver straight to the submerged bomb. Neutralizing the Seaforium requires unscrewing the submerged keg and stirring the chemical solution directly into the explosive powder. The mixture halts the countdown with a soft underwater fizz, stabilizing the charge before the blast can tear through the masonry.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the goal of this quest?",a="You must dive beneath the waters of Loch Modan to the foundation of the Stonewrought Dam, locate the planted keg of Seaforium, and stir in Chief Engineer Hinderweir's disarming mixture to neutralize the blast.",al={"quest objective","what do i do here","a dark threat looms 6 goal"}},{q="Who planted the explosive keg?",a="Dark Iron Insurgents infiltrated the waters of Loch Modan earlier in the day, taking advantage of the absence of local Mountaineers to plant a Seaforium charge directly against the underwater face of the dam.",al={"who put the bomb here","who planted seaforium","dark threat looms culprits"}},{q="What happens if the dam is destroyed?",a="The Stonewrought Dam holds back the massive lake of Loch Modan. If the dam were shattered, millions of gallons of water would flood into the Wetlands and surrounding valleys, washing away roads, towns, and lives.",al={"why save the dam","what happens if the bomb goes off","dam explosion stakes"}},{q="Who concocted the disarming mixture?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII prepared the chemical neutralizer using gathered reagents, creating a mixture capable of neutralizing the Seaforium charge without triggering an accidental detonation.",al={"who made the mixture","hinderweir role","who made the chemical"}},{q="Where is the explosive keg located?",a="The keg is resting underwater against the deep submerged base of the Stonewrought Dam on the southern, lake-facing side.",al={"where is the bomb","keg location","powder keg underwater"}},{q="What kind of explosive was used?",a="The Dark Iron saboteurs utilized Seaforium, a powerful and volatile demolition compound, packed into a sealed waterproof keg.",al={"what is the bomb made of","bomb type","what explosive"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The Stonewrought Dam is an enduring monument of dwarven architecture and pride; protecting it from Dark Iron treachery is of paramount importance to every son and daughter of Ironforge.",["race:Gnome"]="Gnomish minds can appreciate both the sophisticated chemistry behind Hinderweir's neutralizer and the horrifying devastation a Seaforium breach would inflict on dwarven engineering.",["profession:Engineering"]="Working directly with Seaforium and specialized disarming chemicals highlights the extreme, high-stakes application of demolitions and counter-explosive chemistry.",["faction:Alliance"]="The destruction of the Stonewrought Dam would devastate vital transportation routes connecting Khaz Modan to the northern Alliance territories."},kw={"dam","dark iron","disarming","explosive","hinderweir","insurgents","keg","seaforium","stonewrought"},rel={"npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",["end"]="Explosive Charge",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=280},src={"A Dark Threat Looms (6)"}}
E["quest:283"] = {t="quest",n="A Dark Threat Looms",z="lochmodan",s="A Dark Threat Looms is an urgent mission to protect Loch Modan from disaster. Alliance adventurers are tasked with deploying a neutralizing chemical against a planted explosive charge before catastrophic damage can be dealt to the Stonewrought Dam.",h="A Dark Threat Looms is an urgent mission to protect Loch Modan from disaster.",sec={{t="Averted Catastrophe",b="The massive Stonewrought Dam holds back the vast waters of the Loch, towering over the lowlands of the Wetlands below. When Dark Iron saboteurs managed to plant an explosive charge within the structure, the entire valley faced ruin. Applying the Disarming Mixture causes the volatile keg to fizzle harmlessly, defusing the immediate threat to dwarven engineering and countless lives downstream.",sp=0},{t="Hinderweir's Relief",b="Reporting back to Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII brings immense relief to Ironforge's overseers at the site. Hinderweir hails the intervention as a major victory for the Kingdom of Ironforge and the Alliance. Even so, the presence of Dark Iron infiltration so deep into Khaz Modan serves as a grim reminder that their bitter cousins remain relentless in their desire to bring ruin to Ironforge's achievements.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was the goal of this quest chain?",a="The quest chain centers on uncovering and stopping a Dark Iron dwarf sabotage plot aimed at detonating explosives to destroy the Stonewrought Dam.",al={"a dark threat looms summary","stonewrought dam quest goal","why defuse bomb"}},{q="Who planted the explosive charge?",a="Dark Iron dwarven saboteurs planted the explosive keg inside the Stonewrought Dam in an attempt to destroy the massive structure.",al={"who put the bomb here","who attacked the dam","dark irons dam"}},{q="Who is Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII is the dwarven overseer responsible for the maintenance, operation, and defense of the Stonewrought Dam in Loch Modan.",al={"who is hinderweir","hinderweir lore","engineer at the dam"}},{q="What would have happened if the dam broke?",a="If the Stonewrought Dam were breached, the massive reservoir of Loch Modan would drain violently, flooding the Wetlands downstream and washing away roads, settlements, and vital transit routes.",al={"what if dam destroyed","consequences of dam breaking","dam explosion"}},{q="How was the explosive disarmed?",a="A specially concocted Disarming Mixture was poured over the explosive charge, causing the powder keg to fizzle out safely before it could detonate.",al={"how was bomb stopped","disarming mixture","how do you defuse the charge"},sp=1},{q="Is the Stonewrought Dam safe now?",a="While the immediate detonation was prevented and the dam saved, Hinderweir notes that the defense is only secure for the time being, as Dark Iron agents continue to menace the region.",al={"is the dam secure","are the dark irons gone","dam safe forever"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The Stonewrought Dam is a crowning achievement of dwarven stonecraft; protecting it preserves the pride and safety of Ironforge against Dark Iron malice.",["profession:Engineering"]="Neutralizing an unstable demolition device right inside a colossal civil project highlights the vital importance of countermeasures and explosive theory.",["faction:Alliance"]="Preventing the breach of the dam preserves key land corridors between Ironforge and the northern lands of Arathi and Lordaeron."},kw={"dark iron","disarming mixture","explosive charge","hinderweir","loch modan","sabotage","stonewrought dam"},rel={"npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii","subzone:stonewrought-dam","zone:lochmodan","topic:alliance"},m={start="Explosive Charge",["end"]="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=283},src={"A Dark Threat Looms (7)"}}
E["quest:298"] = {t="quest",n="Excavation Progress Report",z="lochmodan",s="Excavation Progress Report is an Alliance errand run from the digs in Loch Modan back to town. Prospector Ironband tasks an adventurer with carrying his latest excavation dispatches and a renewal of his explosive supply orders to Jern Hornhelm in Thelsamar.",h="Excavation Progress Report is an Alliance errand run from the digs in Loch Modan back to town.",sec={{t="A Dispatch to Thelsamar",b="Prospector Ironband's archaeological efforts in Loch Modan require constant logistical support from nearby settlements. Unearthing ancient titan relics is strenuous labor, demanding picks, manpower, and generous quantities of blasting powder to cut through stubborn bedrock. Ironband relies on runners to relay his regular status reports and material requisition orders to Jern Hornhelm, the local expedition contact stationed in Thelsamar.",sp=0},{t="Missing Munitions",b="Upon receiving Ironband's dispatch, Hornhelm learns that the dig site faces severe harassment from aggressive troggs. While Hornhelm agrees that supplying powder to either crack stone or blast troggs is worthy work, Ironband's renewed requisition raises immediate concern. Hornhelm had dispatched a sizable shipment of blastpowder weeks prior, leaving him to wonder what fate befell the missing munitions along the rugged mountain paths.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this report to you?",a="Prospector Ironband gives you the report at Ironband's Excavation Site, located in the southeastern hills of Loch Modan. He is supervising the archaeological dig taking place there.",al={"quest giver","who starts excavation progress report","ironband location"}},{q="Who is Jern Hornhelm?",a="Jern Hornhelm is a dwarven contact for the Explorers' League stationed in Thelsamar. He coordinates local logistics and supplies for archaeological expeditions operating across Loch Modan.",al={"where is jern hornhelm","who is the recipient","thelsamar contact"}},{q="Why does Prospector Ironband need more blastpowder?",a="Ironband ostensibly needs blastpowder to clear solid rock for his excavation. However, the dig site is swarming with hostile troggs, making explosives just as crucial for defense.",al={"why blastpowder","what does ironband want powder for"}},{q="What happened to the previous shipment of powder?",a="Jern Hornhelm sent a shipment of blastpowder weeks ago that never arrived at the excavation. Its mysterious disappearance signals trouble along the supply routes connecting Thelsamar to the outlying sites.",al={"where did the powder go","missing blastpowder"}},{q="What follows after delivering the progress report?",a="After reviewing Ironband's predicament and the unresolved issue of the missing powder, Hornhelm directs you to deliver word of the expedition's status to superiors in Ironforge.",al={"next quest","what comes after","report to ironforge"}},{q="Why are troggs attacking the excavation site?",a="Dwarven excavations often unearth subterranean chambers and disturb trogg dens. The creatures view the miners as intruders on their territory and violently swarm anyone digging into the earth.",al={"trogg attack reason","why troggs hate ironband"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarven adventurers, aiding Ironband upholds the vital historical pursuits of the Explorers' League and protects kin from ravenous trogg incursions.",["profession:Mining"]="Miners understand all too well the necessity of reliable blasting powder when breaking dense bedrock and tunneling into ancient strata.",["faction:Alliance"]="Keeping the supply lines open between Thelsamar and remote outposts ensures Alliance authority remains firm throughout the mountains of Loch Modan."},kw={"blastpowder","excavation progress report","explorers' league","jern hornhelm","loch modan","prospector ironband","thelsamar","trogg"},rel={"npc:prospector-ironband","npc:jern-hornhelm","subzone:thelsamar","quest:301","topic:trogg","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Prospector Ironband",["end"]="Jern Hornhelm",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=298},src={"Excavation Progress Report"}}
E["quest:307"] = {t="quest",n="Filthy Paws",z="lochmodan",s="Filthy Paws is a task given by Mountaineer Stormpike to salvage valuable equipment from the infested Silver Stream Mine. Though depleted of ore, the mine was repurposed as a depot by the Miners' League before encroaching kobolds overran the tunnels. Dwarven authorities want their sturdy tools recovered before the Mountaineers launch a destructive purge of the site.",h="Filthy Paws is a task given by Mountaineer Stormpike to salvage valuable equipment from the infested Silver...",sec={{t="A Depleted Depot",b="The Silver Stream Mine, tucked into the hills of northern Loch Modan east of Algaz Station, yielded its last silver veins long ago. Rather than abandon the subterranean complex, the dwarven Miners' League repurposed the dry shafts as a secure storage depot for spare excavation equipment, picks, and staging materials. Sturdy subterranean tunnels make natural storehouses in Khaz Modan, provided they remain garrisoned and locked against the wilderness.",sp=0},{t="Paws in the Depot",b="Dwarven vigilance has thinned across Loch Modan, and kobolds have seized the opportunity to infiltrate the shafts. Attracted by dark tunnels and the gleaming iron tools left behind, the pests quickly claimed the site as a warren. Mountaineer Stormpike is eager to lead a contingent of warriors into the tunnels to wipe them out, but heavy boots and sweeping cleaves would shatter the crates. An adventurer must sneak or fight their way in to extract the league's supplies before the full-scale assault begins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was gear left in the mine if it had already run dry?",a="The Miners' League converted the Silver Stream Mine into a centralized storage depot after the ore dried up. Subterranean dwarven tunnels provide solid, dry shelters to stockpile bulky tools and supplies until needed elsewhere.",al={"why is gear in silver stream mine","why tools in mine","miners league depot"}},{q="Why doesn't Mountaineer Stormpike clear the mine himself?",a="Stormpike is under orders to wait. Additionally, the Miners' League wants their gear pulled out beforehand; sentry warriors storming into the narrow, dark shafts would likely smash the delicate crated tools in the heat of combat.",al={"why stormpike not going","why mountaineers waiting","stormpike quest reason"}},{q="Where is the Silver Stream Mine located?",a="The mine is located in northern Loch Modan, east of Algaz Station and southwest of the Stonewrought Dam.",al={"silver stream mine location","where is silver stream mine","where filthy paws takes place"}},{q="What makes kobolds so interested in dwarven tools?",a="Kobolds are compulsive subterranean scavengers. They covet metal picks, shovels, candles, and finished ironmongery that make their perpetual burrowing easier, making a warehouse of dwarven tools an irresistible prize.",al={"why do kobolds want gear","kobold tool theft","kobolds silver stream mine"}},{q="Is the Silver Stream Mine dangerous to explore alone?",a="The mine's narrow passageways and dense clusters of kobolds make it hazardous. Mountaineer Stormpike explicitly warns that solitary adventurers may want to bring companions along.",al={"is filthy paws hard","silver stream mine difficulty","can i solo filthy paws"}},{q="Who owns the supplies stored in the mine?",a="The supplies belong to the Ironforge Miners' League, the trade guild responsible for quarrying, mining, and managing subterranean resources across the dwarven kingdom.",al={"who owns the gear","miners league crates","who runs miners league"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, seeing crude kobolds defile the craftsmanship of the Miners' League is an insult that calls for swift reclamation and sharp steel.",["profession:Mining"]="Miners can appreciate the value of high-grade dwarven gear and the tragedy of letting functional tools rust in the paws of cave vermin.",["faction:Alliance"]="With dwarven defensive forces stretched thin across Khaz Modan, clearing supply depots ensures vital infrastructure remains open for the Alliance."},kw={"filthy paws","kobold","loch modan","miners gear","miners' league","mountaineer stormpike","silver stream mine","thelsamar"},rel={"npc:mountaineer-stormpike","subzone:silver-stream-mine","topic:kobold","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Mountaineer Stormpike",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=307},src={"Filthy Paws (Classic)"}}
E["quest:309"] = {t="quest",n="Protecting the Shipment",z="lochmodan",s="Protecting the Shipment is an escort quest in southern Loch Modan where adventurers safeguard the courier Miran on his way to Ironband's Excavation Site. Miran carries a crate of volatile blasting powder urgently needed by Prospector Ironband. The journey exposes lingering Dark Iron subversion threatening the dwarven hinterlands.",h="Protecting the Shipment is an escort quest in southern Loch Modan where adventurers safeguard the courier...",sec={{t="A Powder Run in Peril",b="Prospector Ironband's archaeological dig in the hills of southern Loch Modan requires a steady supply of blasting powder to cut through stubborn stone. When supply lines break down and courier wagons come under threat, the courier Miran is left stranded on the road with a heavy load of powder. Guiding Miran safely across the uneven roads to the excavation site ensures Ironband's work does not stall completely.",sp=0},{t="Dark Iron Sympathizers",b="The road to the dig site is not merely beset by wild beasts; Dark Iron infiltrators actively lie in wait to intercept the explosive cargo. Their brazen ambush near the site reveals a darker truth to Ironband: Dark Iron forces are securing illicit materials and actively sowing discord in the heart of Loch Modan. While the delivery ensures the dig continues, it raises alarm about how deeply enemy sabotage reaches within Alliance territory.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Miran?",a="Miran is an Alliance courier tasked with moving vital supplies, particularly blasting powder, along the dangerous back roads of Loch Modan toward Ironband's Excavation Site.",al={"who is miran","miran loch modan","courier miran"}},{q="Why does Prospector Ironband need the powder?",a="Prospector Ironband leads an important archaeological excavation in southern Loch Modan. His team relies on heavy blasting powder to clear rock, unearth ancient titan artifacts, and sustain their digging operations.",al={"why ironband needs powder","powder purpose","ironband blasting powder"}},{q="Who attacks during the escort?",a="Dark Iron dwarf saboteurs ambush the courier just short of the excavation site, seeking to seize the explosives and thwart Ironforge's operations in the region.",al={"who ambushes miran","ambush attackers","escort attackers"}},{q="Where does the escort lead?",a="The escort begins along the southern road of Loch Modan and concludes at Ironband's Excavation Site, located in the hills southeast of the lake.",al={"escort destination","where does miran go","where is ironband"}},{q="Why are Dark Irons in Loch Modan?",a="The Dark Iron clan maintains secret enclaves and spies throughout Khaz Modan. They actively raid supply lines, sabotage Explorers' League digs, and seek to destabilize Ironforge's defensive perimeter.",al={"dark iron loch modan","why dark iron dwarves here","dark iron presence"}},{q="What happens after the shipment arrives?",a="Prospector Ironband accepts the powder with relief, thanking the Light that the supplies arrived despite the unsettling revelation that Dark Iron sympathizers are operating nearby.",al={"quest continuation","what after protecting the shipment","next quest"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves of Ironforge, defending Ironband's supplies is a direct defense of heritage, protecting ancestral discoveries from the sabotage of their bitter Dark Iron kin.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance relies on clear logistics in Loch Modan; keeping couriers safe from subterranean raiders preserves the link between Ironforge and the eastern frontiers.",["profession:Mining"]="Miners understand all too well the value—and volatility—of blasting powder when carving into Khaz Modan's stubborn bedrock."},kw={"blasting powder","dark iron ambush","ironband's excavation site","loch modan escort","miran","prospector ironband"},rel={"quest:302","npc:prospector-ironband","subzone:ironband-s-excavation-site","quest:436","zone:lochmodan","topic:light"},m={start="Miran",["end"]="Prospector Ironband",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=309},src={"Protecting the Shipment (Classic)"}}
E["quest:418"] = {t="quest",n="Thelsamar Blood Sausages",z="lochmodan",s="In the bustling town of Thelsamar, cook Vidra Hearthstove keeps the local laborers and miners fed with a famous highland staple: blood sausages. Preparing this hearty dwarven fare requires freshly gathered ingredients from the surrounding valley of Loch Modan.",h="In the bustling town of Thelsamar, cook Vidra Hearthstove keeps the local laborers and miners fed with a...",sec={{t="A Hearty Highland Dish",b="Thelsamar is never short on hungry appetites. Between energetic children and weary miners returning from the Ironband Excavation, Vidra Hearthstove works tirelessly over the tavern stove. To keep the populace fed and satisfied, she relies on a local culinary tradition known across Loch Modan: savory blood sausages made from the wildlife wandering the rugged mountain pass.",sp=0},{t="Unconventional Spices",b="While traditional blood sausage relies on fresh blood, seasoned meat, and natural casings, Vidra's recipe reflects the rugged pragmatism of the dwarves. Boar intestines provide the casings, bear meat forms the dense filling, and spider ichor is added to lend a sharp, pungent bite. Though collecting venomous fluid and entrails is not for the faint of heart, the result is a regional favorite that travelers quickly learn to appreciate.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Vidra Hearthstove?",a="Vidra Hearthstove is the resident cook and homemaker in Thelsamar, located within the Stoutlager Inn. She takes immense pride in feeding the hardworking folk of Loch Modan, especially the laborers from nearby excavation sites.",al={"vidra","who is vidra","thelsamar cook"}},{q="Why does the recipe use spider ichor?",a="Vidra uses spider ichor as a distinctive spice to give her blood sausages their signature kick. Dwarven palates are famously hardy, and the venomous fluid lends a pungent flavor that plain herbs cannot match.",al={"spider ichor in sausage","why spider ichor","spider spice"}},{q="Who eats Thelsamar blood sausages?",a="The sausages feed the local townspeople, rambunctious children, and the weary workers returning each evening from grueling shifts at the Ironband Excavation site.",al={"who eats blood sausage","why make sausage"}},{q="Where are the ingredients found?",a="All three components—black bears, mountain boars, and wood lurker spiders—roam the wilderness and wooded hills surrounding the lake across Loch Modan.",al={"where to get bear meat","where to get boar intestines","ingredient locations"}},{q="What casing is used for the sausages?",a="Vidra uses natural casings cleaned from local mountain boars, creating a sturdy shell capable of holding the dense bear meat and seasoned fillings intact over the fire.",al={"sausage casings","boar intestines","casing recipe"}},{q="Do travelers learn to cook these sausages?",a="Yes. If an adventurer brings Vidra the ingredients, she happily shares her recipe, allowing travelers with culinary skills to craft the hearty dwarven dish on their own.",al={"can i cook blood sausage","sausage recipe","cooking recipe"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Gathering ingredients for Vidra rewards aspiring chefs with the authentic recipe for Blood Sausage, expanding their repertoire of hearty field rations.",["race:Dwarf"]="Blood sausage is a quintessential dwarven comfort food, embodying the rugged culinary tastes of Khaz Modan's mountain clans.",["faction:Alliance"]="Supplying Vidra helps keep Thelsamar's local workforce nourished as they maintain key infrastructure and excavate ancient ruins across Loch Modan."},kw={"bear meat","blood sausage","boar intestines","cooking","loch modan","spider ichor","thelsamar","vidra hearthstove"},rel={"npc:vidra-hearthstove","subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Vidra Hearthstove",level="11",faction="Alliance",id=418},src={"Thelsamar Blood Sausages (Classic)"}}
E["quest:436"] = {t="quest",n="Ironband's Excavation",z="lochmodan",s="Ironband's Excavation is an Alliance quest connecting Thelsamar to an ongoing archaeological dig east of the loch. Jern Hornhelm grows suspicious over unexplained supply delays, dispatching an adventurer to discover what stalls Prospector Ironband's team. Upon reaching the dig site, the truth quickly emerges: a relentless horde of troggs has overrun the ruins.",h="Ironband's Excavation is an Alliance quest connecting Thelsamar to an ongoing archaeological dig east of the...",sec={{t="A Slowdown in the Foothills",b="In the town of Thelsamar, Jern Hornhelm monitors shipments sent across Loch Modan to the Explorers' League. Despite a steady stream of provisions and tools, the dig site led by Prospector Ironband has reported minimal progress. Knowing Ironband as an upright, diligent dwarf, Hornhelm fears that something untoward has disrupted the operation rather than mere laziness.",sp=0},{t="The Trogg Infestation",b="Reaching the excavation site tucked into the eastern hills reveals the true cause of the delay. Explorer Magmar Fellhew reports that violent troggs have swarmed the dig site, harassing the dwarven crew and scattering their discoveries. The League cannot complete its study of the ancient stones until the savage intruders are driven back.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Ironband's Excavation?",a="Jern Hornhelm, stationed in Thelsamar, asks you to check on the excavation. He has noticed a lack of progress despite regular deliveries of supplies and wants someone on the ground to investigate.",al={"quest starter","who gives quest","jern hornhelm role"}},{q="Where is the excavation site located?",a="The excavation lies in the foothills east of the loch. Travelers from Thelsamar must skirt the southern end of the water and follow the path eastward into the hills.",al={"dig site location","where is ironbands excavation","how to get there"}},{q="Who is Magmar Fellhew?",a="Magmar Fellhew is an explorer assisting Prospector Ironband at the dig. He oversees the day-to-day operations and logistics on-site and clarifies the situation for messengers sent from Thelsamar.",al={"fellhew","who is magmar fellhew","turn in npc"}},{q="Why has progress stalled at the dig?",a="The expedition has been halted by aggressive troggs. The creatures surged into the ruins, disrupting excavations and forcing the League to divert its focus to self-defense.",al={"why slow","delay reason","what happened to the dig"}},{q="What comes next after completing this quest?",a="Magmar Fellhew directs you to assist the team in reclaiming what was lost, continuing immediately into the quest Gathering Idols to recover relics stolen by the troggs.",al={"next quest","followup","gathering idols quest"}},{q="What is the Explorers' League looking for here?",a="Prospector Ironband's expedition seeks ancient relics and stonework beneath Loch Modan to shed light on dwarven history and their long-lost origins.",al={"excavation purpose","dwarf dig reason","ancient ruins loch modan"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Every dig in Khaz Modan represents an effort to uncover the truth behind dwarven ancestry and Titan heritage, making the safety of Ironband's crew vital to Ironforge.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing Loch Modan requires keeping vital trade roads and research sites free from the subterranean threat of encroaching trogg tribes."},kw={"excavation","explorers league","fellhew","hornhelm","ironband","loch modan","thelsamar","troggs"},rel={"npc:jern-hornhelm","npc:prospector-ironband","zone:lochmodan","topic:trogg","topic:dwarf"},m={start="Jern Hornhelm",["end"]="Magmar Fellhew",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=436},src={"Ironband's Excavation"}}
E["quest:454"] = {t="quest",n="After the Ambush",z="lochmodan",s="After a Dark Iron assault disrupts the delivery of blasting powder to the southern excavation site in Loch Modan, Huldar splits the duties with his partner Miran. Unwilling to risk another ambush alone, Miran requires a sturdy escort to carry the remaining supplies safely to the dig site.",h="After a Dark Iron assault disrupts the delivery of blasting powder to the southern excavation site in Loch...",sec={{t="A Fractured Supply Line",b="Transporting explosive mining powder through the hills of Loch Modan was never simple, but the open hostility of the Dark Iron dwarves turned routine labor into a lethal undertaking. Following an ambush spearheaded by Saean and his conspirators, the haulers Huldar and Miran find their routine shattered. With barrels scattered and the road perilous, the pair must divide their efforts: Huldar guards what remains behind, while Miran prepares to push forward with the next load.",sp=0},{t="The Road to the Dig",b="The excavation sites across Loch Modan depend on steady deliveries of blasting powder to break stone and unearth titan relics. Miran knows well that another ambush could erupt from any ridge along the path. By securing a traveling companion before strapping down his cargo, the hauler hopes to bypass whatever lurking traps the Dark Irons still hold in reserve.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are Huldar and Miran?",a="Huldar and Miran are dwarven haulers tasked with moving heavy barrels of blasting powder across Loch Modan to support local excavation efforts.",al={"who is huldar","who is miran","powder haulers loch modan"}},{q="Why can't Huldar and Miran travel together?",a="Following an ambush along their route, the shipment was left vulnerable. They divided their responsibilities so Huldar can stay behind and guard the remaining barrels while Miran moves forward with the first batch.",al={"why split up","why split powder"}},{q="Who attacked the shipment?",a="A group of hostile Dark Iron dwarves led by Saean ambushed the haulers, attempting to disrupt Alliance operations and seize or destroy their mining explosives.",al={"who ambushed them","who is saean"}},{q="Where is Miran taking the powder?",a="Miran is hauling the barrels to the southern excavation site in Loch Modan, where Prospector Ironband's team requires blasting powder to clear rock and uncover buried ruins.",al={"where is powder going","miran destination"}},{q="Why is blasting powder so heavily guarded in Loch Modan?",a="Blasting powder is crucial for the Explorers' League excavations, but in the wrong hands, it poses an immense danger. Dark Iron infiltrators operating throughout the region actively seek to sabotage supplies and disrupt Ironforge's hold on the territory.",al={"why protect blasting powder","powder importance"}},{q="What happens after talking to Miran?",a="Once Miran completes his final checks on the wagon and cargo, he asks you to escort him along the roadway to ensure the shipment reaches the excavation site intact.",al={"next step after the ambush","what does miran do"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Defending Ironforge's logistics from treacherous Dark Iron saboteurs directly preserves the safety of your homeland's mountain passes and mining operations.",["faction:Alliance"]="Keeping the supply lines open in Loch Modan ensures that the League's research continues and the southern passes remain under Alliance control.",["profession:Mining"]="Blasting powder is the lifeblood of deep subterranean digs, making the protection of these barrels essential to any serious mining venture."},kw={"ambush","blasting powder","dark iron","excavation","huldar","loch modan","miran","saean"},rel={"npc:huldar","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Huldar",["end"]="Miran",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=454},src={"After the Ambush"}}
E["quest:455"] = {t="quest",n="The Algaz Gauntlet",z="lochmodan",s="The Algaz Gauntlet is an urgent military mission to fight through Dun Algaz, a critical mountain pass linking Loch Modan to the Wetlands. Orcs of the Dragonmaw clan have entrenched themselves in the tunnels, threatening to sever Ironforge's vital lifeline to Menethil Harbor. Adventurers are tasked with cutting down the orcish vanguard and delivering word of the invasion to Valstag Ironjaw.",h="The Algaz Gauntlet is an urgent military mission to fight through Dun Algaz, a critical mountain pass linking...",sec={{t="A Severed Artery",b="Dun Algaz serves as the solitary overland mountain pass carving through the crags between Loch Modan and the marshy basin of the Wetlands. For the dwarves of Ironforge, this stone corridor is essential for trade, troop movements, and supplies heading to Menethil Harbor, the Alliance's primary coastal port in the region. Should the pass fall, Ironforge's connection to the western seas is effectively strangled, leaving isolated outposts cut off from dwarven reinforcements.",sp=0},{t="The Dragonmaw Surge",b="While remnants of the Dragonmaw clan have long haunted the hills and ruins of the Wetlands following the Second War, their sudden, organized push into Dun Algaz marks an aggressive escalation. Instead of lingering in their marshland enclaves, Dragonmaw scouts and grunts have seized the tunnels and fortified the pass. Mountaineer Rockgar enlists brave Alliance travelers to shatter this blockade by slaying the encroaching orcs and carrying word of the assault directly to Valstag Ironjaw in Menethil Harbor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Dun Algaz so important to the Alliance?",a="Dun Algaz is the only direct mountain highway connecting Loch Modan to the Wetlands. It links the heart of Khaz Modan to Menethil Harbor, the main Alliance port facilitating naval transport across the seas.",al={"why dun algaz matters","dun algaz importance","why clear the pass"}},{q="Who are the Dragonmaw orcs occupying the pass?",a="The Dragonmaw clan are remnants of the Old Horde who notoriously enslaved red dragons during the Second War. Following their defeat, scattered factions retreated into the Wetlands, and they have now pushed south into the pass to claim strategic choke points.",al={"who are the dragonmaw","why are orcs in dun algaz","dragonmaw clan lore"}},{q="Where does this mission lead?",a="Once you fight through the pass and eliminate the occupying grunts and scouts, the road leads north through the Wetlands and turns west at the fork toward Menethil Harbor, where you report to Valstag Ironjaw.",al={"where do i go after algaz gauntlet","who gets the report","where is valstag ironjaw"}},{q="Why is Valstag Ironjaw surprised by the report?",a="The Dragonmaw typically keep to hidden camps in the marshy hills of the Wetlands. Their bold surge into the dwarven tunnels of Dun Algaz represents an unexpected and alarming shift toward organized aggression.",al={"valstag reaction","why did orcs attack algaz"}},{q="Who orders the assault on the pass?",a="Mountaineer Rockgar, a dwarven guard stationed at the northern border of Loch Modan, orders the strike to prevent the orcs from solidifying their foothold and cutting off communication with the coast.",al={"who gives the quest","mountaineer rockgar mission"}},{q="What comes after completing this gauntlet?",a="Delivering the report to Valstag Ironjaw alerts the garrison at Menethil Harbor to the immediate threat, opening further opportunities to aid the dwarven defense against the Dragonmaw in the Wetlands.",al={"next quest after algaz gauntlet","what to do in menethil"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Clearing Dun Algaz protects the ancestral mountain passes of Khaz Modan and preserves critical access between Ironforge and its western sea harbor.",["faction:Alliance"]="Menethil Harbor is the Alliance's primary gateway between the Eastern Kingdoms and western lands; keeping the overland route clear is essential for the entire faction."},kw={"dragonmaw","dun algaz","loch modan","menethil harbor","pass","rockgar","valstag ironjaw","wetlands"},rel={"quest:468","subzone:dun-algaz","npc:valstag-ironjaw","topic:dragonmaw-clan","zone:lochmodan","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor"},m={start="Mountaineer Rockgar",["end"]="Valstag Ironjaw",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=455},src={"The Algaz Gauntlet"}}
E["quest:468"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Mountaineer Rockgar",z="lochmodan",s="Report to Mountaineer Rockgar is an Alliance breadcrumb quest directing adventurers north from the guard posts of Loch Modan toward Dun Algaz. Mountaineer Kadrell dispatches capable travelers to join Rockgar, who is organizing a vital expedition into the sodden lowlands of the Wetlands. It serves as the gateway passage connecting the dwarven homeland to northern territories.",h="Report to Mountaineer Rockgar is an Alliance breadcrumb quest directing adventurers north from the guard...",sec={{t="The Road to the North Gate",b="Dun Algaz represents the crucial artery between Loch Modan and the marshy expanses of the Wetlands. Built into the northern mountain ridge, the fortified pass has long guaranteed safe passage for trade, messengers, and military detachments moving between Ironforge and Alliance settlements further north. With tensions rising along the borders, Mountaineer Kadrell keeps a close watch on travellers passing through, recruiting hardy volunteers to reinforce the northern outposts.",sp=0},{t="A Mission Gone Awry",b="While Mountaineer Kadrell initially sends recruits expecting an ordinary scouting expedition, the reality at Dun Algaz proves far more hazardous. Upon arriving at the northern gate, adventurers find Mountaineer Rockgar preparing for active conflict rather than a peaceful reconnaissance trek. Hostile forces choking the pass quickly turn what was meant to be simple scouting into a bitter, messy struggle to secure the gauntlet.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the order to report to Rockgar?",a="Mountaineer Kadrell gives the task. Stationed in Thelsamar across the road from the Stoutlager Inn, he keeps watch over the main road leading toward the mountain pass.",al={"who starts report to mountaineer rockgar","quest giver rockgar","kadrell quest"}},{q="Where can I find Mountaineer Rockgar?",a="Mountaineer Rockgar is stationed north along the road out of Loch Modan, guarding the entrance to the mountain tunnels of Dun Algaz.",al={"rockgar location","where is rockgar","mountaineer rockgar spot"}},{q="Why is this mission through Dun Algaz so important?",a="Dun Algaz is the primary overland corridor linking Loch Modan to the Wetlands. Keeping the passage clear is vital for the Alliance to maintain supply chains, military communication, and safe travel to Menethil Harbor and beyond.",al={"why go to dun algaz","dun algaz importance","wetlands route"}},{q="What happens after meeting Mountaineer Rockgar?",a="Rockgar enlists your help immediately for The Algaz Gauntlet, revealing that the intended scouting operation has turned into a bloody fight to clear out the hostile forces blocking the mountain tunnels.",al={"what comes after report to rockgar","rockgar follow up","next quest after rockgar"},sp=1},{q="What level of adventurer should take on this assignment?",a="This assignment is aimed at seasoned travelers around level 20 to 21 who are finishing their duties across Loch Modan and preparing to brave the perilous Wetlands.",al={"rockgar quest level","level for dun algaz","when to go to wetlands"}},{q="Is this quest available to Horde characters?",a="No. The Ironforge Mountaineers are strictly loyal to King Magni Bronzebeard and the Alliance, meaning only Alliance adventurers can accept the quest.",al={"can horde do this quest","horde report to rockgar"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Answering the call of fellow mountaineers reinforces the vital overland link between the Ironforge heartland and the dwarven holdings in the Wetlands.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing Dun Algaz ensures uninterrupted overland transit to Menethil Harbor, the Alliance's primary western port in the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"dun algaz","ironforge","kadrell","loch modan","mountaineer","rockgar","scouting","wetlands"},rel={"quest:455","subzone:dun-algaz","npc:mountaineer-kadrell","zone:lochmodan","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Mountaineer Kadrell",["end"]="Mountaineer Rockgar",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=468},src={"Report to Mountaineer Rockgar"}}
E["quest:6387"] = {t="quest",n="Honor Students",z="lochmodan",s="Mining instructor Brock Stoneseeker rewards promising young apprentices in Thelsamar with honorary mining picks. To arrange delivery of the tools from Ironforge, he directs adventurers to enlist the aid of the local gryphon master, Thorgrum Borrelson.",h="Mining instructor Brock Stoneseeker rewards promising young apprentices in Thelsamar with honorary mining...",sec={{t="A Miner's Due",b="In the dwarf town of Thelsamar, mining is more than an occupation—it is a cornerstone of daily survival and dwarven pride. Brock Stoneseeker watches dozens of fresh recruits pass through his training, drilling them on rock composition and tunnel safety. For the students who distinguish themselves above the rest, tradition demands recognition in the form of a finely crafted honorary pick. Because local supply is limited, obtaining these picks requires reaching across Khaz Modan into the heart of Ironforge.",sp=0},{t="Taking to the Skies",b="Rather than trusting the slow, mountainous trek back through Dun Morogh on foot, Brock relies on the kingdom's aerial courier network. Thorgrum Borrelson tends the gryphon roost perched beside Thelsamar, offering rapid transit to the capital. Handing Brock's order to Thorgrum initiates a courier run that connects rural frontier training directly to the grand foundries of the dwarven capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Brock Stoneseeker?",a="Brock Stoneseeker is a mining instructor residing in Thelsamar. He trains novices in the foundational skills of excavation and stonecraft.",al={"brock stoneseeker","who is brock","mining trainer thelsamar"}},{q="Why does Brock need picks from Ironforge?",a="Brock compiles a list of high-achieving mining students who have earned honorary picks. To fulfill these rewards, the order must be delivered to Golnir Bouldertoe, a mining supplies vendor stationed in Ironforge.",al={"why ironforge","why picks","brock's list"}},{q="What role does Thorgrum Borrelson play in this task?",a="Thorgrum Borrelson is Thelsamar's gryphon master. Brock instructs couriers to bring the order list to him so they can arrange speedy aerial transport back to Ironforge.",al={"thorgrum borrelson","who is thorgrum","gryphon master thelsamar"}},{q="Who receives the list in Ironforge?",a="The list is ultimately destined for Golnir Bouldertoe in Ironforge, who prepares the ceremonial picks for Brock's accomplished students.",al={"who gets the list","golnir bouldertoe","ironforge contact"}},{q="Where does this errand lead next?",a="Once you speak with Thorgrum Borrelson, he arranges a gryphon flight directly to Ironforge so you can hand-deliver the order to Golnir Bouldertoe.",al={"next step","what follows honor students","after brock's list"}},{q="Where does this task take place?",a="The task begins and concludes within the settlement of Thelsamar, located along the rolling hills of Loch Modan.",al={"quest location","where is thelsamar","where to start honor students"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The errand highlights dwarven respect for mining as a disciplined craft, where mastering stone and vein earns tangible recognition from master instructors.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarven adventurers, this task reflects the tight bond between frontier settlements like Thelsamar and the capital's deep mountain halls.",["faction:Alliance"]="This request introduces travelers in Loch Modan to the Alliance's vital network of flight masters and aerial couriers."},kw={"brock stoneseeker","golnir bouldertoe","gryphon","honor students","ironforge","loch modan","mining","thelsamar","thorgrum borrelson"},rel={"npc:brock-stoneseeker","npc:thorgrum-borrelson","npc:golnir-bouldertoe","subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Brock Stoneseeker",["end"]="Thorgrum Borrelson",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6387},src={"Honor Students (Classic)"}}
E["quest:8642"] = {t="quest",n="Silvervein the Elder",z="lochmodan",s="Silvervein the Elder is an honored ancestral spirit who appears during the Lunar Festival atop the hills overlooking Thelsamar in Loch Modan. Travelers pay their respects to him to honor the ancient ties among Azeroth's elder peoples. In return for acknowledging his presence and heritage, he bestows his ancestral blessing.",h="Silvervein the Elder is an honored ancestral spirit who appears during the Lunar Festival atop the hills...",sec={{t="A Vigil Over Thelsamar",b="Perched on the rolling ridges above Thelsamar, Elder Silvervein stands as a quiet guardian and reminder of antiquity. As a figure honored during the Lunar Festival, he represents the enduring memories of bygone eras. Even as the surrounding lands of Loch Modan grapple with trogg invasions and local disputes, Silvervein watches peacefully from his overlook.",sp=0},{t="Honoring the Olden Races",b="The presence of spirits like Silvervein serves to bridge the divide between modern folk and ancient lineages. When adventurers seek him out, he expresses gratitude that travelers still pay homage to the olden races of Azeroth. His greeting carries the warmth of ancestral appreciation, offering a commemorative token to those who honor him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Silvervein?",a="Elder Silvervein is an ancestral spirit who manifests during the Lunar Festival. He spends the festival resting atop the high bluffs near Thelsamar in Loch Modan.",al={"silvervein","who is silvervein","elder silvervein loch modan"}},{q="Where can I find Elder Silvervein?",a="He is located on a grassy hill overlooking the town of Thelsamar within Loch Modan.",al={"silvervein location","where is elder silvervein","find silvervein"}},{q="What is the purpose of seeking out Elder Silvervein?",a="Adventurers seek him out during the Lunar Festival to pay their respects to the ancestors and ancient races, receiving a festive token and blessing in return.",al={"why visit silvervein","what does silvervein do","silvervein purpose"}},{q="What does he mean by 'the olden races'?",a="He refers to the ancient peoples of Azeroth who lived and shaped the world long before modern conflicts took center stage, honoring the enduring spirit of their heritage.",al={"olden races meaning","why olden races"}},{q="Is Elder Silvervein friendly to Horde travelers?",a="Yes. Ancestral elders honored during the Lunar Festival welcome travelers of all backgrounds who come in peace to honor the ancestors.",al={"can horde talk to silvervein","horde silvervein"}},{q="Does Elder Silvervein have any connection to the trogg invasion?",a="No. While Loch Modan is beset by trogg incursions and excavator troubles, Elder Silvervein remains entirely separate from local military conflicts, focused purely on ancestral reverence.",al={"silvervein troggs","is silvervein fighting troggs"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Resting right beside the dwarven settlement of Thelsamar, Elder Silvervein shares an appreciative bond with the rugged stonefolk and their reverence for ancient history.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers passing through Loch Modan, ascending the ridge above Thelsamar offers a quiet respite from trogg hunting to honor the ancient dead."},kw={"ancestor","coin of ancestry","elder","loch modan","lunar festival","silvervein","thelsamar"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Elder Silvervein",id=8642},src={"Silvervein the Elder"}}
E["subzone:algaz-station"] = {t="subzone",n="Algaz Station",z="lochmodan",s="Algaz Station is a dwarven military outpost situated in northwestern Loch Modan, directly south of the fortified pass of Dun Algaz. Manning the approach to the northern tunnels, its garrison of Mountaineers helps safeguard travelers and watch the frontier leading toward the Wetlands.",h="Algaz Station is a dwarven military outpost situated in northwestern Loch Modan, directly south of the...",sec={{t="Watching the Northern Pass",b="Perched just east of North Gate Pass and south of Dun Algaz, Algaz Station serves as a vital strategic watchpoint for the kingdom of Ironforge. A cadre of dwarven Mountaineers maintains a permanent vigil here, keeping the vital road between Loch Modan and the northern lowlands open to trade and troop movements. Given the frequent threats in the surrounding hills, from wandering beasts to encroaching troggs, the outpost provides respite, repairs, and martial support for weary travelers before they venture through the mountain tunnels.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Algaz Station?",a="It is an Ironforge military outpost in northwestern Loch Modan. It serves as a guard post and waystation for Mountaineers patrolling the mountain passes leading north to Dun Algaz.",al={"what is this place","algaz station purpose","who runs algaz station"}},{q="Where does the station get its name?",a="It takes its name from Dun Algaz, the massive dwarven pass and tunnel system situated just north of the station that connects Loch Modan to the Wetlands.",al={"why is it called algaz station","dun algaz connection","name meaning"}},{q="Who can be found at Algaz Station?",a="The outpost is manned by dwarven Mountaineers, including Mountaineer Stormpike, alongside support personnel like the armorer Gothor Brumn who provides field repairs to travelers.",al={"who is here","npcs at algaz station","mountaineer stormpike location"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarven travelers, Algaz Station is a familiar emblem of Ironforge's reach, ensuring the king's highways remain guarded against threats spilling from the mountains.",["faction:Alliance"]="The outpost offers a secure staging ground and repair stop for Alliance adventurers journeying between Loch Modan and the marshlands of the north."},kw={"algaz station","dun algaz","gothor brumn","ironforge","loch modan","mountaineer stormpike","mountaineers","north gate pass"},rel={"subzone:dun-algaz","zone:lochmodan","subzone:north-gate-pass","npc:mountaineer-stormpike"},src={"Algaz Station"}}
E["subzone:farstrider-lodge"] = {t="subzone",n="Farstrider Lodge",z="lochmodan",s="Tucked away in the southeastern hills of Loch Modan, Farstrider Lodge is a tranquil hunting outpost built in high elven style. Though founded as an elven waystation, it now serves travelers, rangers, and trappers of all Alliance races looking to test their skills against the local wildlife.",h="Tucked away in the southeastern hills of Loch Modan, Farstrider Lodge is a tranquil hunting outpost built in...",sec={{t="An Elven Haven in the Mountains",b="Farstrider Lodge stands apart from the sturdy stone and timber works typical of Khaz Modan. Bearing the graceful curves and vaulted woodwork of high elven craftsmanship, the outpost is named after the Farstriders, the renowned rangers of Quel'Thalas. Long before the recent wars shattered the elven homeland, Farstriders ranged far south of their borders to explore and build ties with the wider world. While only a solitary high elf remains to tend the lodge today, its hunting heritage endures under the stewardship of local dwarves and human woodsmen.",sp=0},{t="A Waystation for the Wilds",b="Situated high on the bluffs overlooking the loch, the lodge serves as a base of operations for hunters, scouts, and trappers navigating the untamed corners of the zone. Between offering training for marksmen and shelter from roaming beasts, the lodge remains closely tied to the nearby settlement of Thelsamar, ensuring that supplies and wilderness intelligence flow freely between the dwarven mountaineers and the woodsmen guarding the southeastern frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is there an elven lodge in Khaz Modan?",a="Farstrider Lodge was established long before the recent wars by the Farstriders, the ranger corps of Quel'Thalas, who sought to maintain a presence and build ties across the wider world beyond their northern kingdom.",al={"why elven building loch modan","who built farstrider lodge","why high elf lodge here"}},{q="Are there still high elves living here?",a="Only a single high elf ranger, Vyrin Swiftwind, currently resides at the lodge. The rest of the occupants are dwarven mountaineers and human huntsmen who maintain the lodge and trade with travelers.",al={"are there high elves here","who lives in farstrider lodge","vyrin swiftwind"}},{q="What services are available at Farstrider Lodge?",a="The lodge primarily supports outdoorsmen, providing a hunter trainer, a pet trainer, local merchants, and rest for wilderness scouts tracking dangerous wildlife across the loch.",al={"what is at farstrider lodge","hunter trainers loch modan"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Farstrider Lodge is a prime sanctuary for hunters, offering both mentorship in marksmanship and beast training amidst the rich game of Loch Modan's surrounding hills.",["race:Dwarf"]="Though built by elven hands, the lodge operates in close harmony with the mountaineers of Thelsamar to monitor the dangerous wildlife threatening Khaz Modan."},kw={"farstrider lodge","farstriders","high elf","hunter lodge","loch modan","thelsamar","vyrin swiftwind"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","subzone:thelsamar","topic:dwarf"},src={"Farstrider Lodge"}}
E["subzone:grizzlepaw-ridge"] = {t="subzone",n="Grizzlepaw Ridge",z="lochmodan",s="Grizzlepaw Ridge is a rugged, craggy hillside rising south of Thelsamar in Loch Modan. It is notorious among local mountaineers for its dense population of wild bears, led by the legendary beast Ol' Sooty.",h="Grizzlepaw Ridge is a rugged, craggy hillside rising south of Thelsamar in Loch Modan.",sec={{t="Home of the Bears",b="Overlooking the road south of Thelsamar and bordering Stonesplinter Valley to the west, Grizzlepaw Ridge is rough country dominated by predatory wildlife. The slopes are claimed by territorial bears that pose a hazard to travelers skirting the mountains. Deep within the ridge dwells Ol' Sooty, a massive and unusually fierce bear feared by local hunters. Travelers moving between the dwarven settlements must keep a wary eye on the tree line and rocky terraces above.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Grizzlepaw Ridge located?",a="Grizzlepaw Ridge lies in the central hills of Loch Modan, directly south of the town of Thelsamar and east of the trogg-infested Stonesplinter Valley.",al={"where is grizzlepaw ridge","grizzlepaw ridge location","how to get to grizzlepaw ridge"}},{q="What dangerous creatures live on Grizzlepaw Ridge?",a="The ridge is crawling with aggressive bears. Its most infamous resident is Ol' Sooty, an exceptionally large and ferocious beast that occasionally prowls down toward the mountain base.",al={"bears at grizzlepaw ridge","who is ol sooty","ol sooty loch modan"}},{q="Who is Gorick Guzzledraught?",a="Gorick Guzzledraught is a dwarf found in the area, keeping an eye on the surrounding wilderness and the dangerous wildlife roaming the hillside.",al={"gorick guzzledraught","dwarf on grizzlepaw ridge"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The ridge provides a classic proving ground for tracking wild beasts and confronting apex predators like Ol' Sooty.",["race:Dwarf"]="Perched right beside Thelsamar, the ridge's bear population represents a constant nuisance to local mountaineers and supply routes."},kw={"bears","gorick guzzledraught","grizzlepaw ridge","loch modan","ol' sooty","sooty","thelsamar"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","subzone:thelsamar","subzone:stonesplinter-valley"},src={"Grizzlepaw Ridge"}}
E["subzone:ironband-s-excavation-site"] = {t="subzone",n="Ironband's Excavation Site",z="lochmodan",s="Ironband's Excavation Site is an expansive dwarven dig located in southeastern Loch Modan, just south of the lake and southwest of Farstrider Lodge. Led by Prospector Ironband, the archaeological operation was abruptly halted when aggressive, volatile troggs overran the trenches.",h="Ironband's Excavation Site is an expansive dwarven dig located in southeastern Loch Modan, just south of the...",sec={{t="Unearthing the Past",b="Spurred by the dwarven drive to uncover their ancient Titan origins, Prospector Ironband established this sprawling digsite along the rugged cliffs of southeastern Loch Modan. What began as a promising excavation quickly turned into a disaster when the digging disturbed an unusually fierce and large breed of subterranean troggs. The creatures surged from the earth, driving back the miners and setting up camp amidst the scattered tools, broken carts, and half-excavated relics.",sp=0},{t="Ruins in the Red Earth",b="Much like archaeological efforts in the Badlands, Wetlands, and Uldaman, the site sits in dangerous limbo. Surviving prospectors cling to the edges of the perimeter, desperate to reclaim their stolen gear and protect exposed artifacts—including strange ancient statues left behind by long-forgotten builders—from being smashed or carried off by the ravenous trogg infestation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Ironband's Excavation Site located?",a="The excavation site is located in the southeastern region of Loch Modan, directly south of the Loch and southwest of Farstrider Lodge.",al={"ironband location","where is ironbands digsite","ironband map"}},{q="Who is Prospector Ironband?",a="Prospector Ironband is an archaeologist and explorer heading up the excavation on behalf of the dwarven Explorers' League, attempting to salvage artifacts and drive back the local troggs.",al={"who is ironband","prospector ironband lore"}},{q="Why is the excavation site overrun with troggs?",a="As the dwarven miners excavated deeper into the soil of Loch Modan, their tunneling breached subterranean pockets inhabited by a large and aggressive breed of troggs, who quickly overwhelmed the workers and seized the site.",al={"why are troggs here","who attacked the digsite","ironband troggs"}},{q="What were the dwarves hoping to find here?",a="Like many dwarven archaeological digs across Khaz Modan, the miners were searching for ancient Titan relics and stone ruins that might shed light on the ancestral origins of the dwarven race.",al={"what are they digging for","ironband artifacts","why dig here"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The overrun dig is a stinging setback for the Explorers' League, who view the recovery of ancient relics here as vital to understanding dwarven heritage.",["profession:Mining"]="The quarry and open pits showcase typical dwarven heavy-extraction techniques, though ongoing trogg hostility makes any prospecting hazardous."},kw={"digsite","excavation site","explorers league","ironband","loch modan","prospector ironband","troggs"},rel={"npc:prospector-ironband","quest:436","zone:lochmodan","subzone:farstrider-lodge","topic:trogg","topic:dwarf","subzone:uldaman","subzone:the-loch"},src={"Ironband's Excavation Site"}}
E["subzone:mo-grosh-stronghold"] = {t="subzone",n="Mo'grosh Stronghold",z="lochmodan",s="Mo'grosh Stronghold is a fortified den of ogres dug into the northeastern hills of Loch Modan. Nestled among ancient, weathered ruins, these brutal giants pose a constant threat to the dwarven settlements below.",h="Mo'grosh Stronghold is a fortified den of ogres dug into the northeastern hills of Loch Modan.",sec={{t="A Looming Threat",b="Tucked away in the crags of northeastern Loch Modan, Mo'grosh Stronghold serves as the primary base for the Mo'grosh clan of ogres in the region. The brute forces lurking within the caves and outer camps raid traveling dwarven supply caravans and present an enduring danger to the peace of Thelsamar. The rugged stonework scattered around the camp suggests the site once belonged to an older settlement, likely trolls, before the lumbering ogres claimed the territory and raised their distinctive mounds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Mo'grosh Stronghold?",a="It is an ogre compound built into the hills of northeastern Loch Modan. The Mo'grosh ogres inhabit the caves and surrounding grounds, forming the largest hostile ogre enclave in the territory.",al={"mogrosh stronghold","ogre camp loch modan","mogrosh cave"}},{q="Who used to live here before the ogres?",a="The ancient stonework around the stronghold indicates it was once an old troll settlement. It remains uncertain whether the Mo'grosh ogres drove the trolls out through violence or simply took over ruins that had long been abandoned.",al={"ancient ruins loch modan","who built mogrosh","trolls in loch modan"}},{q="Why are the ogres a problem for the dwarves?",a="Their proximity to key travel routes makes them a severe hazard to local traffic and trade caravans moving through Loch Modan. Dwarven authorities regularly call upon adventurers to thin their numbers and keep the mountain passes safe.",al={"why kill mogrosh ogres","ironforge threat mogrosh"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The Mo'grosh ogres constantly menace dwarven patrols and travelers, making the eradication of their stronghold a matter of civic defense for the Mountaineers of Loch Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing Loch Modan requires keeping the Mo'grosh ogres in check, ensuring safe passage between Ironforge and the northern mountain roads."},kw={"loch modan","mo'grosh","mogrosh","mountaineers","ogre","ruins","stronghold"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","topic:troll"},src={"Mo'grosh Stronghold"}}
E["subzone:north-gate-pass"] = {t="subzone",n="North Gate Pass",z="lochmodan",s="North Gate Pass is a vital mountain thoroughfare connecting the snowy crags of Dun Morogh with the rolling basin of Loch Modan. It forms the northern corridor through the Khaz Modan peaks, watched over by a fortified dwarven outpost. Travelers heading toward the northern lowlands of the Wetlands frequently traverse this high road.",h="North Gate Pass is a vital mountain thoroughfare connecting the snowy crags of Dun Morogh with the rolling...",sec={{t="Gateway Between the Peaks",b="Carved into the sheer stone of Khaz Modan, North Gate Pass serves as the northern arterial link between the high, frozen valleys of Dun Morogh and the temperate waters of Loch Modan. Descending through steep mountain tunnels, travelers emerging from the west are greeted by the broad expanse of the loch valley. Because it sits within easy striking distance of the paths heading down into the Wetlands, the pass carries heavy traffic of dwarven messengers, merchants, and roaming adventurers. Its strategic value is anchored by the North Gate Outpost, where mountaineers keep vigilant watch against troggs and mountain predators.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does North Gate Pass lead?",a="The pass connects eastern Dun Morogh to northwestern Loch Modan. Following the road further north around the loch leads toward the mountain tunnels descending into the Wetlands, making it a critical junction for northern travelers.",al={"where does north gate pass go","north gate pass destination","path through north gate pass"}},{q="What guards the pass?",a="The Ironforge Mountaineers maintain North Gate Outpost directly along the road, monitoring travelers and keeping the mountain passage clear of prowling beasts and roaming troggs.",al={"who guards north gate pass","north gate pass guards","dwarf outpost north gate"}},{q="How does this differ from South Gate Pass?",a="Both passes link Dun Morogh to Loch Modan through carved tunnels, but North Gate Pass lies to the north, offering the most direct overland route for travelers moving onward toward the Wetlands and northern lands.",al={"difference north and south gate pass","north gate vs south gate"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves journeying between the high gates of Ironforge and the frontier settlements around The Loch, the pass is a familiar, stone-hewn threshold guarded by fellow mountaineers.",["faction:Alliance"]="The pass represents a crucial military and supply corridor connecting the dwarven capital to northern Alliance expeditions bound for the Wetlands."},kw={"dun morogh","ironforge","loch modan","mountaineers","north gate outpost","north gate pass","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:north-gate-outpost","zone:lochmodan","zone:dunmorogh","zone:wetlands","subzone:the-loch"},src={"North Gate Pass"}}
E["subzone:silver-stream-mine"] = {t="subzone",n="Silver Stream Mine",z="lochmodan",s="Silver Stream Mine is a depleted dwarf mine located in northern Loch Modan, nestled between Algaz Station and the Stonewrought Dam. Once a rich silver vein for the kingdom of Ironforge, the excavated hollow was repurposed as a Miners' League supply depot before being overrun by vermin. Today, Tunnel Rat kobolds squat inside the tunnels, hoarding stolen equipment and rare mineral curiosities.",h="Silver Stream Mine is a depleted dwarf mine located in northern Loch Modan, nestled between Algaz Station and...",sec={{t="From Rich Vein to Storage Depot",b="Silver Stream Mine once flowed with precious ore, contributing heavily to the silver reserves of Ironforge. In time, the dwarf pickaxes dug deep enough to exhaust the primary veins, turning the sprawling chambers into an empty subterranean complex. Rather than abandon the hard-won earthworks, the Miners' League transformed the shafts into a secure storage depot for tools, mining crates, and regional equipment. It also serves as the only known source of rare Charged Rift Gems, which draw inquisitive arcanists searching for delicate tailoring reagents.",sp=0},{t="The Kobold Incursion",b="The quiet depot did not remain secure for long. Aggressive Tunnel Rat kobolds, drawn by the smell of unattended tools, candle wax, and forgotten subterranean crevices, swarmed the shafts in large numbers. The Miners' League caretakers were promptly driven out into the Loch Modan cold. Now, the kobolds guard the stolen dwarf crates with manic fervor, while old, shattered orcish catapults and wagons rest forgotten outside the rear entrances, silent reminders of older frontier skirmishes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Silver Stream Mine originally used for?",a="Originally, it was a productive silver mine excavated by the dwarves of Ironforge. After the veins ran dry, the Ironforge Miners' League repurposed the vacant subterranean halls into a storage depot for tools and excavation supplies.",al={"what is silver stream mine","silver stream history","why was silver stream built"}},{q="Who currently occupies the mine?",a="The mine has been completely overrun by Tunnel Rat kobolds. They chased off the dwarf caretakers and now guard the tunnels, hoarding the League's abandoned supply crates and digging for residual scraps.",al={"who lives in silver stream mine","silver stream mobs","what is inside silver stream mine"}},{q="Why do mages travel to Silver Stream Mine?",a="The mine is the only known source of Charged Rift Gems. These volatile, magically reactive stones are sought after by Alliance arcanists to weave potent enchanted robes.",al={"mage quest silver stream","charged rift gems","silver stream mage robes"}},{q="What are the ruined catapults behind the mine?",a="Behind the mine sit broken orcish wagons and ruined catapults, weathered remnants of earlier wartime conflicts that threatened the passages connecting Loch Modan and the northern mountain passes.",al={"orc wagons behind silver stream","broken catapults loch modan mine","horde siege engines loch modan"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Silver Stream Mine is an infuriating loss of hard-earned infrastructure, where clumsy kobolds now sully a respectable Ironforge Miners' League depot.",["class:Mage"]="Apprentice mages journey into the dangerous kobold-infested tunnels specifically to extract Charged Rift Gems, an indispensable ingredient for crafting ritual garments."},kw={"charged rift gem","kobold","loch modan","miners league","silver stream mine","tunnel rat"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","quest:307","quest:1961","topic:kobold","subzone:algaz-station","subzone:stonewrought-dam","zone:ironforge","topic:alliance"},src={"Silver Stream Mine"}}
E["subzone:south-gate-outpost"] = {t="subzone",n="South Gate Outpost",z="lochmodan",s="South Gate Outpost is a fortified dwarven mountain post situated along the South Gate Pass between Dun Morogh and Loch Modan. Manning the snowy southern road, its mountaineers guard the steady flow of travelers walking between Ironforge's frigid heights and the temperate valley of the Loch.",h="South Gate Outpost is a fortified dwarven mountain post situated along the South Gate Pass between Dun Morogh...",sec={{t="Watchers of the Southern Road",b="Perched midway through the high mountain cut of South Gate Pass, South Gate Outpost marks the frontier between the snowy slopes of Dun Morogh and the verdant basin of Loch Modan. Stationed here are Ironforge mountaineers tasked with patrolling the rocky switchbacks and keeping dangerous wildlife off the main highway. Compared to their hard-pressed kin up at North Gate Outpost, the defenders here have largely secured their stretch of road, allowing travelers, pilgrims, and trade wagons headed toward Thelsamar to journey in relative safety.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of South Gate Outpost?",a="It serves as a fortified border checkpoint and garrison along South Gate Pass. Mountaineers stationed here keep the snowy transit road clear of mountain beasts and hostile interlopers traveling between Dun Morogh and Loch Modan.",al={"why is south gate outpost here","south gate outpost purpose","what is south gate outpost"}},{q="Why is it so much calmer here than at North Gate Outpost?",a="The garrison at South Gate Outpost has successfully culled the aggressive wildlife immediately bordering the road. North Gate Outpost, by contrast, contends with heavier incursions and wilder mountain terrain, leaving the southern pass comparatively calm.",al={"difference between north gate and south gate","is south gate safe","south gate vs north gate"}},{q="Where does the road through South Gate Outpost lead?",a="Heading westward up the pass brings you into the snowy highlands of Dun Morogh toward Ironforge. Traveling eastward downhill leads directly out into the temperate valley of Loch Modan, with the road winding straight toward the settlement of Thelsamar.",al={"where does this road go","south gate road destination","south gate pass path"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves leaving Coldridge Valley and Dun Morogh for the first time, South Gate Outpost is the final chilly landmark before descending into the vibrant, sunlit lands of Loch Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="The outpost serves as a dependable military shelter along one of Khaz Modan's primary domestic supply lines, keeping the passage between the capital and eastern settlements open."},kw={"dun morogh","dwarf","ironforge road","loch modan","mountaineers","south gate outpost","south gate pass","thelsamar"},rel={"subzone:south-gate-pass","zone:lochmodan","zone:dunmorogh","subzone:thelsamar","subzone:north-gate-outpost","subzone:the-loch"},src={"South Gate Outpost"}}
E["subzone:south-gate-pass"] = {t="subzone",n="South Gate Pass",z="lochmodan",s="South Gate Pass is the primary mountain thoroughfare linking the snowy heights of Dun Morogh with the valley basin of Loch Modan. Flanked by dwarven tunnels and watch posts, it serves as the most direct route between Ironforge and the settlement of Thelsamar.",h="South Gate Pass is the primary mountain thoroughfare linking the snowy heights of Dun Morogh with the valley...",sec={{t="The Road East",b="Carved straight through the Khaz Modan range, South Gate Pass connects Dun Morogh's high mountains to the rolling valley of Loch Modan to the east. Travelers leaving the cold slopes behind emerge through stone archways into the warmer dwarven heartlands. Because the path leads straight toward Thelsamar, it carries a steady flow of mountaineers, couriers, and newly trained adventurers setting out from the capital.",sp=0},{t="A Guarded Threshold",b="The pass is fortified against wild beasts and prowling troggs by the South Gate Outpost, where dwarven mountaineers maintain a constant watch. Though generally safer than the untamed wilds deeper in the valley, travelers are advised to keep to the road, as hostile wildlife and roving threats frequently probe the approaches.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does South Gate Pass lead?",a="Heading west through the tunnels brings you into the snowy highlands of Dun Morogh, on the road toward Ironforge. Traveling east leads down into the basin of Loch Modan, directly toward the settlement of Thelsamar.",al={"where does south gate pass go","south gate pass destination","south gate road"}},{q="Is South Gate Pass safe to travel?",a="The road itself is relatively secure thanks to the dwarven guards stationed at South Gate Outpost, but bears, spiders, and encroaching troggs inhabit the surrounding crags and hillsides outside the tunnel mouth.",al={"is south gate pass dangerous","south gate pass threats"}},{q="Why is this pass used more than North Gate Pass?",a="South Gate Pass provides the most direct and convenient overland connection between Dun Morogh and Thelsamar, making it the preferred route for local trade, supply caravans, and travelers heading into central Loch Modan.",al={"south gate vs north gate","why use south gate"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves leaving Dun Morogh, South Gate Pass is the threshold where the icy mountain air gives way to the open valleys and quarries of Loch Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="The pass serves as a vital internal artery connecting Ironforge with the eastern Alliance territories, maintained and secured by the King's Mountaineers."},kw={"dun morogh","loch modan","mountaineers","south gate outpost","south gate pass","thelsamar","tunnel"},rel={"subzone:south-gate-outpost","subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan","zone:dunmorogh"},src={"South Gate Pass"}}
E["subzone:stonesplinter-valley"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonesplinter Valley",z="lochmodan",s="Stonesplinter Valley is a rugged mountain vale in southwestern Loch Modan overrun by hostile troggs. Once a pristine alpine hollow, it has transformed into a fortified encampment under the brute command of the trogg chieftain Grawmug.",h="Stonesplinter Valley is a rugged mountain vale in southwestern Loch Modan overrun by hostile troggs.",sec={{t="A Chittering Stronghold",b="Tucked away among the craggy slopes of southwestern Loch Modan, Stonesplinter Valley was once a quiet alpine hollow. That serenity ended when waves of subterranean troggs clawed their way to the surface across Khaz Modan. Claiming the valley for their own, the Stonesplinter tribe rapidly turned the rocky defiles into crude fortifications, digging dens, erecting barricades, and hunting anything that strays too close. Their numbers make the valley an open wound on the southern road toward the wetlands and the southern passes, forcing Mountaineers out of Thelsamar to hire adventurous mercenaries willing to cull their ranks and eliminate their towering warlord, Grawmug.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Stonesplinter Valley located?",a="It is carved into the mountains in the southwestern corner of Loch Modan, just south of the main road heading past the Grizzlepaw Ridge.",al={"stonesplinter valley location","where is stonesplinter valley","trogg valley loch modan"}},{q="Who rules Stonesplinter Valley?",a="The encampment is dominated by a brutish trogg chieftain named Grawmug, who directs the tribe's raids on local travelers and patrols from the deepest recess of the valley.",al={"who leads the stonesplinter troggs","grawmug","trogg boss loch modan"}},{q="Why are the troggs here in Loch Modan?",a="Troggs were unearthed deep underground during dwarven excavations elsewhere in Khaz Modan. Driven by senseless aggression, separate warbands migrated to the surface, and the Stonesplinter tribe chose this secluded mountain vale as their primary staging ground.",al={"why are there troggs in loch modan","where did the troggs come from","trogg origin loch modan"}},{q="Why do the dwarves care about clearing the valley?",a="The valley sits dangerously close to dwarf settlements, mines, and mountain roads. Leaving an entrenched army of Stonesplinter troggs unchecked threatens the safety of travelers moving through southern Loch Modan and strains the already stretched Mountaineer patrols.",al={"why fight stonesplinter troggs","thelsamar trogg problem"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The trogg infestation here is an insult to the security of Loch Modan, and the Mountaineers of Thelsamar rely on stout dwarven kin to clear out Grawmug's encroaching brutes.",["faction:Alliance"]="Clearing out Stonesplinter Valley secures vital supply routes running through Loch Modan, which have grown vulnerable with Ironforge forces stretched thin across the realm."},kw={"grawmug","loch modan","stonesplinter","stonesplinter valley","thelsamar","troggs"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","topic:trogg"},src={"Stonesplinter Valley"}}
E["subzone:stonewrought-dam"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonewrought Dam",z="lochmodan",s="The Stonewrought Dam is a colossal dwarven engineering marvel standing along the northern rim of Loch Modan. It holds back the waters of the Loch, creating the massive highland lake while draining the Wetlands below into habitable marshes.",h="The Stonewrought Dam is a colossal dwarven engineering marvel standing along the northern rim of Loch Modan.",sec={{t="A Wonder of Dwarven Craft",b="Stretching across the canyon east of Dun Algaz, the Stonewrought Dam is widely regarded as one of the great structural triumphs of dwarven civilization. Designed by the master Dark Iron architect Franclorn Forgewright, the barrier was built using his pioneering stonewrought technique. By trapping the waters of the mountain basin, the dam doubled the surface area of the Loch while steadily lowering water levels to the north, allowing the marshy basin of the Wetlands to emerge from a once completely flooded valley.",sp=0},{t="Sabotage and Defense",b="Though built under the guidance of a Dark Iron architect, the dam today serves Ironforge—and has become a prime target for Dark Iron saboteurs operating out of the southern mountains. Recent assaults and infiltration attempts have forced Ironforge to station a garrison here under Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII. Guards and engineers patrol the masonry day and night, knowing that any breach would catastrophically drain the Loch and unleash a devastating deluge across the Wetlands below.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who built the Stonewrought Dam?",a="It was designed and overseen by the famous Dark Iron architect Franclorn Forgewright, who invented the stonewrought construction technique. Although built by a Dark Iron master, it serves the Bronzebeard kingdom today.",al={"who made stonewrought dam","creator of the dam","dam architect"}},{q="What happens if the dam breaks?",a="A collapse would be catastrophic. The Loch would rapidly drain and leave Loch Modan an empty crater of mud, while the displaced water would sweep down into the Wetlands as an uncontrollable, devastating flood.",al={"if dam breaks","what if the dam breaks","dam destroyed"}},{q="Why are Dark Iron dwarves attacking it?",a="The Dark Iron clan seeks to strike at Ironforge's vital infrastructure and destabilize the region. Crippling the dam would cripple supply lines, drown the northern wetlands, and strike a bitter blow against Bronzebeard pride.",al={"why attack dam","dark iron dam attack"}},{q="Who is currently in charge of the dam's defense?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII manages the day-to-day operations and defensive fortifications of the dam, coordinating with Ironforge forces to weed out saboteurs.",al={"who runs the dam","dam engineer"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The dam stands as a monument to ancient dwarven masonry and architectural ingenuity, though its Dark Iron heritage remains a sore and contested point among Ironforge's historians.",["profession:Engineering"]="For engineers of any stripe, the dam is a masterclass in hydraulic control and stonewrought load-bearing mechanics, rivaling even the great works beneath Ironforge."},kw={"dark iron","franclorn forgewright","hinderweir","loch modan","stonewrought dam","the loch","wetlands"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","subzone:the-loch","zone:wetlands","npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii","topic:dark-iron-clan","subzone:dun-algaz","zone:ironforge","topic:dwarf"},src={"Stonewrought Dam"}}
E["subzone:stoutlager-inn"] = {t="subzone",n="Stoutlager Inn",z="lochmodan",s="The Stoutlager Inn is the lively heart of Thelsamar and a primary haven for travelers in Loch Modan. Tucked beneath the rolling hills of the loch, it offers warm hearths, strong dwarven ale, and a bustling gathering place for adventurers and locals alike.",h="The Stoutlager Inn is the lively heart of Thelsamar and a primary haven for travelers in Loch Modan.",sec={{t="A Welcoming Hearth in the Hills",b="Situated squarely in the settlement of Thelsamar, the Stoutlager Inn serves as the center of community life for southern Loch Modan. Miners, mountaineers, and wayfarers passing between Dun Morogh and the Wetlands stop here to trade rumors, secure lodging, and share hearty drafts of dwarven brew. While the wilderness beyond Thelsamar grows increasingly hostile with trogg and gnoll activity, the thick stone walls and roaring fires of the Stoutlager provide a dependable sanctuary.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What services are available at the Stoutlager Inn?",a="The inn provides traditional tavern amenities, including an innkeeper to bind hearthstones, beds for weary travelers, and local merchants offering provisions and drinks to sustain journeys across Loch Modan.",al={"inn services","what is in the inn","thelsamar innkeeper"}},{q="Where is the Stoutlager Inn located?",a="It is built right in the center of Thelsamar, the primary Alliance town situated in western Loch Modan along the main roadway.",al={"inn location","where is stoutlager","find stoutlager inn"}},{q="Why is the inn so important to Thelsamar?",a="Beyond offering food and lodging, the Stoutlager Inn acts as the town square and news hub. It is where local mountaineers post bounties and travelers plan excursions into the surrounding hills.",al={"why is it popular","thelsamar tavern lore"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For Bronzebeard dwarves, the Stoutlager Inn embodies the familiar warmth of home, renowned for genuine hospitality, fresh ale, and reliable companionship away from Ironforge.",["faction:Alliance"]="The inn serves as a crucial staging ground and safe haven for Alliance adventurers heading north toward the Wetlands or patrolling the troubled valleys around the loch."},kw={"dwarf","hearthstone","innkeeper","loch modan","stoutlager inn","tavern","thelsamar"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","zone:lochmodan"},src={"Stoutlager Inn"}}
E["subzone:the-loch"] = {t="subzone",n="The Loch",z="lochmodan",s="The Loch is the vast freshwater lake that dominates the valley of Loch Modan. Held back by the monumental Stonewrought Dam, it is the largest body of water on Khaz Modan and the lifeblood of the surrounding dwarven settlements.",h="The Loch is the vast freshwater lake that dominates the valley of Loch Modan.",sec={{t="Heart of the Valley",b="Spanning the center of Loch Modan, The Loch is among the largest inland lakes in the known world, rivaled only by Lordamere Lake and Darrowmere Lake in the north. Its waters support local fishermen and provide a peaceful backdrop for the town of Thelsamar and nearby hunting lodges. Beneath its calm surface, however, prowl aggressive threshadons and freshwater beasts that make swimming across a perilous venture.",sp=0},{t="The Stonewrought Barrier",b="The Loch exists in its current tranquil state thanks to masterwork dwarven engineering. To the north stands the massive Stonewrought Dam, an architectural marvel built across the mountain cleft to prevent the lake from flooding out into the Wetlands below. Maintaining this colossal structure is essential to preserving the valley's ecosystem and keeping Khaz Modan secure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is The Loch?",a="The Loch is the massive mountain lake that fills the center of the Loch Modan valley in Khaz Modan. It is one of the largest bodies of freshwater in the world and defines the geography and livelihood of the local dwarves.",al={"the loch lore","what is the loch lake","loch modan lake"}},{q="How does the lake stay full?",a="The lake is contained to the north by the Stonewrought Dam, a towering dwarven construction. The dam holds back countless gallons of water that would otherwise spill down through the mountain pass into the low-lying Wetlands.",al={"why doesn't the loch drain","what holds the loch back","stonewrought dam purpose"}},{q="Is it safe to swim in The Loch?",a="Not entirely. While local fishermen dot the shores and piers, deeper waters are home to predatory threshadons and snapping beasts that frequently attack unwary travelers venturing far from land.",al={"loch monsters","swimming the loch","creatures in the loch"}},{q="How large is The Loch compared to other lakes?",a="It is the largest body of water on the continent of Khaz Modan and the third largest known lake in the Eastern Kingdoms, behind only Lordamere Lake and Darrowmere Lake in Lordaeron.",al={"biggest lake","the loch size comparison","how big is the loch"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The Loch is a centerpiece of Ironforge pride, demonstrating how dwarven masonry and the Stonewrought Dam can tame nature to sustain settlements like Thelsamar.",["faction:Alliance"]="The tranquil waters of The Loch provide vital freshwater and trade routes between Ironforge's central valley and the surrounding outposts."},kw={"khaz modan","lake","loch modan","stonewrought dam","the loch","thelsamar","threshadon","wetlands"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","subzone:stonewrought-dam","zone:wetlands","subzone:darrowmere-lake"},src={"The Loch"}}
E["subzone:thelsamar"] = {t="subzone",n="Thelsamar",z="lochmodan",s="Thelsamar is the primary dwarven settlement in Loch Modan, nestled on the western bluffs overlooking the great lake. Positioned along the main road between Dun Morogh and the Wetlands, it serves as a bustling hub of commerce, hospitality, and civic defense against surrounding trogg and ogre incursions.",h="Thelsamar is the primary dwarven settlement in Loch Modan, nestled on the western bluffs overlooking the...",sec={{t="Heart of Loch Modan",b="Thelsamar serves as the central bastion of dwarven civilian life in the valley. Built with traditional Khaz Modan stone and timber architecture, it features the lively Stoutlager Inn, a dedicated gryphon roost, crafting stations, and various supply merchants. Sitting directly on the thoroughfare connecting the South Gate Pass into Dun Morogh with the North Gate Pass toward the Wetlands, almost all travelers through the region pass beneath its warm hearths and stout roofs.",sp=0},{t="Trouble on the Frontier",b="Despite its cozy comforts, Thelsamar is in constant danger. To the south, troggs pouring from Stonesplinter Valley threaten the town's perimeter, while bears and predatory beasts haunt Grizzlepaw Ridge. With Ironforge's regular military forces stretched thin across the realm, the local magistrate and Mountaineers rely heavily on traveling adventurers and mercenaries to patrol the trade roads and beat back encroaching hostiles.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What services are available in Thelsamar?",a="Thelsamar offers a full suite of frontier amenities, including the Stoutlager Inn for lodging and refreshment, a flightmaster with connections across central Khaz Modan, trade vendors, and an outdoor forge. It also hosts several profession and combat trainers to assist growing adventurers.",al={"thelsamar vendors","what is in thelsamar","trainers in thelsamar"}},{q="Where does the road through Thelsamar lead?",a="The north-south road running west of the town connects south through the tunnel into Dun Morogh, leading straight toward Ironforge. Following it north takes travelers across the Stonewrought Dam and through the Algaz Gate down into the marshy Wetlands.",al={"thelsamar road","where does the path go","travel from thelsamar"}},{q="Why is the town hiring so many mercenaries?",a="The local Mountaineers are overwhelmed by multiple emerging threats. Aggressive Stonesplinter troggs have overrun the southern excavations, wild beasts prowl the edges of settlement, and organized ogres have begun pressing in, forcing town leadership to offer bounties to independent fighters.",al={"why are there quests in thelsamar","who is attacking thelsamar"}},{q="What is the famous local specialty here?",a="The town is renowned among hunters and travelers for Thelsamar Blood Sausages, a rich dwarven dish prepared by Vidra Hearthstove at the Stoutlager Inn using the entrails and flesh of local wildlife.",al={"thelsamar food","blood sausages loch modan"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves leaving cold Dun Morogh, Thelsamar is the first taste of warmer lowlands, boasting great ale, stout stone hearths, and active service to the Mountaineer guard.",["profession:Cooking"]="Culinary travelers often stop at the Stoutlager Inn to learn the regional recipe for hearty blood sausages made from the meat of local bears, spiders, and boars."},kw={"blood sausages","grizzlepaw","loch modan","mountaineers","stonesplinter","stoutlager inn","thelsamar"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","subzone:stoutlager-inn","subzone:the-loch","quest:418","quest:255","quest:256","subzone:stonesplinter-valley","subzone:grizzlepaw-ridge"},src={"Thelsamar"}}
E["subzone:valley-of-kings"] = {t="subzone",n="Valley of Kings",z="lochmodan",s="The Valley of Kings is a lush canyon nestled in the southwestern corner of Loch Modan, directly south of the passage to Dun Morogh. It serves as a heavily watched gateway into the fiery Searing Gorge, flanked by monumental stone figures carved in memory of the War of the Three Hammers. Travelers venturing here walk beneath ancient dwarven history while facing the immediate threat of Blackrock encroachers and troggs.",h="The Valley of Kings is a lush canyon nestled in the southwestern corner of Loch Modan, directly south of the...",sec={{t="Guardians of the Southern Pass",b="The valley's most commanding feature is the pair of colossal statues depicting King Madoran Bronzebeard and High Thane Khardros Wildhammer. Carved by joint commission from their sons following their deaths, these stone titans overlook the pass into the scorched southlands. They stand as a lasting monument to the allied victory in the War of the Three Hammers and an eternal warning against the Dark Iron clan, reminding all who look south of the ruin brought upon the Redridge Mountains by the summoning of Ragnaros.",sp=0},{t="The Gate to the Searing Gorge",b="Beyond serving as a path between South Gate Pass and Stonesplinter Valley, the Valley of Kings holds the heavy iron gate leading down into the Searing Gorge. Because of the hostile Blackrock orcs, Dark Iron dwarves, and volcanic hazards lurking on the other side, the gate is kept strictly locked and guarded by Ironforge mountaineers. Mountaineer Pebblebitty keeps watch over the threshold, turning away all but the hardiest adventurers who can prove they possess the strength to survive the inferno beyond.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who do the two giant statues represent?",a="The two immense statues depict King Madoran Bronzebeard of Ironforge and High Thane Khardros Wildhammer. Their sons commissioned the monuments together following their fathers' deaths to celebrate the alliance that triumphed in the War of the Three Hammers.",al={"statues in valley of kings","dwarf statues loch modan","who are the statues"}},{q="Why were the statues built facing south?",a="They were erected to gaze directly toward the southern territories shattered by the Dark Iron clan's summoning of Ragnaros. The twin kings stand as a protective shield and an enduring warning to the Dark Irons and any other hostile force attempting to invade the northern dwarven lands.",al={"why statues look south","purpose of statues","statues facing searing gorge"}},{q="How do I get through the locked gate at the southern end?",a="The gate leading into the Searing Gorge is kept locked for traveler safety. You must speak with Mountaineer Pebblebitty, who stands guard at the gate, and prove your capabilities by undertaking a task for her before she will provide the key to pass through.",al={"how to open searing gorge gate","mountaineer pebblebitty key","valley of kings gate locked"}},{q="Where does this valley lead?",a="The valley connects the South Gate Pass leading to Dun Morogh, the trogg-infested Stonesplinter Valley to the east, and the blazing badlands of the Searing Gorge through the heavily fortified southern gate.",al={"valley of kings connections","where does valley go"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves of Ironforge, the Valley of Kings is hallowed ground showcasing the unbreakable bond forged between Bronzebeard and Wildhammer against the treachery of the Dark Irons.",["faction:Alliance"]="The valley acts as the northern bulwark against the gathering threats of the Redridge badlands, keeping the smoldering perils of the Searing Gorge from spilling into peaceful Khaz Modan."},kw={"khardros wildhammer","loch modan","madoran bronzebeard","pebblebitty","searing gorge gate","valley of kings","war of the three hammers"},rel={"zone:lochmodan","zone:searinggorge","subzone:south-gate-pass","subzone:stonesplinter-valley","zone:dunmorogh"},src={"Valley of Kings"}}
E["zone:lochmodan"] = {t="zone",n="Loch Modan",z="lochmodan",s="Loch Modan is a temperate mountain valley east of Dun Morogh, renowned for its massive alpine lake held in place by the monumental Stonewrought Dam. Centered around the dwarven town of Thelsamar, the region struggles under encroaching trogg infestations, kobolds in the mines, and aggressive ogres in the northeast highlands.",h="Loch Modan is a temperate mountain valley east of Dun Morogh, renowned for its massive alpine lake held in...",sec={{t="A Highland Jewel",b="Situated in eastern Khaz Modan, Loch Modan presents a stark, pleasant contrast to the frozen snowfields of Dun Morogh. Rugged mountain peaks enclose a temperate valley of pine and birch, cradling the Loch itself. This massive body of fresh water is held in place by the Stonewrought Dam, an architectural triumph that towers along the northern rim. The peaceful settlement of Thelsamar serves as the civic heart of the territory, housing traveling mountaineers, hunters, and miners who ply the productive veins of copper and tin scattered throughout the hills.",sp=0},{t="Unearthed Terrors and Invasions",b="Loch Modan's tranquil scenery conceals recurrent violence. Broken catapults and ballistae resting on the lake bed remain from the Second War, when the orcish Horde occupied the valley before the dwarves drove them out. More recently, dwarven archaeological excavations accidentally unearthed subterranean swarms of savage troggs. Led by savage chieftains, trogg tribes have overrun the southern canyons of Stonesplinter Valley and the Valley of Kings, threatening trade routes and forcing the Ironforge Mountaineers to wage a desperate defense.",sp=0},{t="Plots in the Shadows",b="Troggs and the hulking ogres of Mo'grosh Stronghold are not the only dangers encroaching on the valley. Deeper investigations into local sabotages reveal that the treacherous Dark Iron dwarves are operating in Loch Modan. Having made incursions from the burning passes to the south, Dark Iron infiltrators target dwarven blastpowder reserves and harbor sinister designs against the Stonewrought Dam itself.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What holds the lake back from flooding the Wetlands?",a="The Stonewrought Dam, a massive wonder of dwarven stonework and engineering, holds back the entire Loch. Dwarven engineers maintain it meticulously, as its failure would wash out the lower marshlands of the Wetlands to the north.",al={"what is the dam","stonewrought dam purpose","why does loch modan have a dam"}},{q="Where did all the troggs come from?",a="Dwarven exploratory expeditions and miners accidentally breached underground chambers deep in the mountains, unleashing hordes of savage troggs that quickly swarmed to the surface and carved out camps in the valleys.",al={"why are there troggs here","trogg invasion loch modan","trogg origin"}},{q="What is the primary Alliance settlement in the zone?",a="Thelsamar, nestled on the western bluffs, serves as the main Alliance town and travel hub, featuring the Stoutlager Inn, tradesfolk, and gryphon masters connecting to Ironforge and beyond.",al={"loch modan town","hub in loch modan","thelsamar"}},{q="Who rules Mo'grosh Stronghold?",a="The stronghold in the northeast mountains is held by brute ogres who descended into the valley, establishing a fortified micro-dungeon outpost that terrorizes nearby hunters and travelers.",al={"ogre camp loch modan","ogres northeast loch modan","mogrosh"}},{q="What happened to Ironband's Excavation Site?",a="Prospector Ironband's archaeological dig was overrun by troggs spilling out from the subterranean chambers, forcing the excavation team to abandon their progress and fight to secure their remaining supplies.",al={"ironbands dig","why was ironbands site abandoned","prospector ironband problem"}},{q="Can you travel from Loch Modan to the Badlands or Searing Gorge?",a="Yes. Footpaths lead south through the mountains into the arid wasteland of the Badlands, while the Stonewrought Pass through the Valley of Kings leads southwest into the volcanic crags of Searing Gorge.",al={"loch modan to badlands","loch modan south exit","path to badlands"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Loch Modan represents both the unmatched engineering genius of dwarven masonry and the dangerous ancient history your people repeatedly uncover beneath the stone.",["class:Hunter"]="The Farstrider Lodge along the southeastern ridges offers a renowned gathering place for trackers hunting the valley's bears, crocolisks, and mountain buzzards.",["profession:Mining"]="The hills, quarries, and trogg-infested caves of Loch Modan are rich in accessible veins of copper, tin, and silver.",["faction:Alliance"]="Guarding the line between Dun Morogh and the northern routes toward the Wetlands, Loch Modan is a vital bulwark for Ironforge's territorial defense."},kw={"farstrider lodge","ironband","mo'grosh stronghold","stonesplinter","stonewrought dam","the loch","thelsamar","troggs","valley of kings"},rel={"subzone:thelsamar","subzone:stonewrought-dam","zone:dunmorogh","zone:wetlands","subzone:mo-grosh-stronghold","subzone:ironband-s-excavation-site","quest:161","quest:217"},m={levels="10-20"},src={"Loch Modan (Classic)","Loch Modan"}}
